# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In previous lessons, you studied the noise that arises in quantum hardware and worked through current techniques for suppressing and mitigating it. This lesson takes the next step along the path from error mitigation to error correction: instead of actively correcting detected errors, we detect them and discard the runs they touched.\n"
msgstr "Dalam pelajaran sebelumnya, anda telah mempelajari hingar yang timbul dalam perkakasan kuantum dan meneliti teknik semasa untuk menindas serta memitigasinya. Pelajaran ini mengambil langkah seterusnya sepanjang laluan daripada mitigasi ralat kepada pembetulan ralat: daripada membetulkan ralat yang dikesan secara aktif, kita mengesannya dan membuang larian yang terjejas.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<IBMVideo id=\"135063108\" title=\"In this video, Chris Porter describes methods for detecting quantum errors, including parity checks, basic stabilizer checks, and coherent Pauli checks. The text below provides more detail.\"/>\n"
msgstr "<IBMVideo id=\"135063108\" title=\"Dalam video ini, Chris Porter menerangkan kaedah untuk mengesan ralat kuantum, termasuk semakan pariti, semakan penstabil asas dan semakan Pauli koheren. Teks di bawah memberikan butiran lanjut.\"/>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We call this **post-selected quantum error correction**. A set of checks is attached to the circuit, a run that fails a check is flagged as containing an error and discarded, and the accepted runs are used as they are. Nothing is decoded and nothing is corrected, so this workflow does not require real-time decoding or recovery; the price is paid in discarded shots instead. Throughout this lesson, error detection means this post-selected form. [Section 1.1](#symmetry-post-selection) is the limiting case with no code at all: the check is a symmetry of the ideal output, read directly from the measured bits. Beginning with [Section 1.2](#stabilizer-code), the checks are stabilizer measurements on ancilla qubits, first the $[[4,2,2]]$ error-detecting code at the end of the circuit, then coherent Pauli checks and spacetime checks placed around and inside the payload.\n"
msgstr "Kita menamakannya **pembetulan ralat kuantum pasca-pilih**. Satu set semakan dilampirkan pada litar, larian yang gagal dalam semakan ditandakan sebagai mengandungi ralat dan dibuang, dan larian yang diterima digunakan seadanya. Tiada apa-apa yang dinyahkod dan tiada apa-apa yang dibetulkan, jadi aliran kerja ini tidak memerlukan penyahkodan atau pemulihan masa nyata; harganya dibayar melalui shot yang dibuang. Sepanjang pelajaran ini, pengesanan ralat bermaksud bentuk pasca-pilih ini. [Seksyen 1.1](#symmetry-post-selection) ialah kes had tanpa kod langsung: semakannya ialah simetri output unggul, dibaca terus daripada bit yang diukur. Bermula dengan [Seksyen 1.2](#stabilizer-code), semakannya ialah pengukuran penstabil pada qubit ancilla, mula-mula kod pengesan ralat $[[4,2,2]]$ di hujung litar, kemudian semakan Pauli koheren dan semakan ruang-masa yang diletakkan di sekeliling dan di dalam muatan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Quantum error mitigation and quantum error correction (QEC) are often framed as tools for different eras of quantum computing: mitigation for today's devices and correction for scalable fault tolerance. IBM&reg; instead describes [a continuous path from error mitigation to error correction](https://www.ibm.com/quantum/blog/qec-continuum), along which removing errors trades time (samples) against space (qubits). At one end, we have error suppression and mitigation. Some of these techniques are low-overhead. But others, like Probabilistic error cancellation (PEC), pay a sampling cost that grows quickly, even exponentially with the noise in the system. At the other end, full quantum error correction can make a computation reliable in a single shot, but large-scale fault-tolerant architectures require substantial qubit and gate overhead; their connectivity, error-rate, and decoding requirements depend on the code and architecture. Post-selected error correction sits between them, and spacetime codes can make it hardware-efficient by distributing low-weight Pauli checks across both space and time in a circuit. The [Qiskit Paulice](https://www.ibm.com/quantum/blog/qiskit-paulice) addon lets you place such checks in your own circuits today (see its [documentation](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/addons/qiskit-addon-paulice)). In [this blog post](https://www.ibm.com/quantum/blog/qec-continuum), IBM reports that a recent demonstration encoded 64 logical qubits in spacetime codes on 76 physical qubits, in a circuit that also contained 314 $T$ gates, and gave roughly a tenfold effective improvement in gate error rates after post-selection.\n"
msgstr "Mitigasi ralat kuantum dan pembetulan ralat kuantum (QEC) sering dianggap sebagai alat untuk era pengkomputeran kuantum yang berbeza: mitigasi untuk peranti hari ini dan pembetulan untuk toleransi kerosakan berskala. IBM&reg; sebaliknya menggambarkan [laluan berterusan daripada mitigasi ralat kepada pembetulan ralat](https://www.ibm.com/quantum/blog/qec-continuum), yang di sepanjangnya penyingkiran ralat menukar masa (sampel) dengan ruang (qubit). Di satu hujung, terdapat penindasan dan mitigasi ralat. Sesetengah teknik ini beroverhed rendah. Tetapi yang lain, seperti Probabilistic error cancellation (PEC), membayar kos pensampelan yang meningkat dengan pantas, malah secara eksponen dengan hingar dalam sistem. Di hujung yang satu lagi, pembetulan ralat kuantum penuh boleh menjadikan pengiraan boleh dipercayai dalam satu shot, tetapi seni bina toleran kerosakan berskala besar memerlukan overhed qubit dan gate yang besar; keperluan kesambungan, kadar ralat dan penyahkodannya bergantung pada kod dan seni bina. Pembetulan ralat pasca-pilih terletak di antara keduanya, dan kod ruang-masa boleh menjadikannya cekap perkakasan dengan mengagihkan semakan Pauli berat rendah merentasi ruang dan masa dalam litar. Addon [Qiskit Paulice](https://www.ibm.com/quantum/blog/qiskit-paulice) membolehkan anda meletakkan semakan sedemikian dalam litar anda sendiri hari ini (lihat [dokumentasinya](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/addons/qiskit-addon-paulice)). Dalam [catatan blog ini](https://www.ibm.com/quantum/blog/qec-continuum), IBM melaporkan bahawa satu demonstrasi terkini mengekod 64 qubit logik dalam kod ruang-masa pada 76 qubit fizikal, dalam litar yang turut mengandungi 314 gate $T$, dan memberikan peningkatan berkesan kira-kira sepuluh kali ganda dalam kadar ralat gate selepas pasca-pemilihan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The basic protocol is as follows. One first selects a detection strategy. Depending on the strategy, the original circuit is either augmented with additional gates that implement an explicit consistency check (placed internally in the circuit, or at the end), or, when the ideal output obeys a known constraint, the circuit is run unchanged and that constraint serves as the check. The (augmented) circuit is then executed and measured, and the check outcomes, or the structural constraint evaluated on the measured bitstrings, are used to flag shots as likely corrupted and reject them in classical post-processing (or recover the correct state probabilistically, as in configuration recovery). The aim is to improve the accepted samples, at the cost of fewer usable shots, and the benefit must be checked against the errors introduced by the detection circuit.\n"
msgstr "Protokol asasnya adalah seperti berikut. Pertama, satu strategi pengesanan dipilih. Bergantung pada strategi tersebut, litar asal sama ada ditambah dengan gate tambahan yang melaksanakan semakan konsistensi yang jelas (diletakkan di dalam litar, atau di hujung), atau, apabila output unggul mematuhi kekangan yang diketahui, litar dijalankan tanpa perubahan dan kekangan itu berfungsi sebagai semakan. Litar (yang ditambah) kemudian dilaksanakan dan diukur, dan hasil semakan, atau kekangan struktur yang dinilai pada rentetan bit yang diukur, digunakan untuk menandakan shot sebagai berkemungkinan rosak dan menolaknya dalam pemprosesan pasca klasik (atau memulihkan keadaan yang betul secara kebarangkalian, seperti dalam pemulihan konfigurasi). Tujuannya ialah memperbaik sampel yang diterima, dengan kos shot yang boleh digunakan lebih sedikit, dan manfaatnya mesti disemak terhadap ralat yang diperkenalkan oleh litar pengesanan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This lesson builds up to spacetime codes through a continuum of post-selection techniques, starting from the simplest &mdash; a symmetry rule on the measured bitstring &mdash; and ending with checks whose detection regions reach deep into the circuit's interior. In the hardware examples in Parts 1 and 2, we weigh the gain from post-selection against its cost in added gates and discarded shots.\n"
msgstr "Pelajaran ini membina ke arah kod ruang-masa melalui kontinum teknik pasca-pemilihan, bermula daripada yang paling mudah &mdash; peraturan simetri pada rentetan bit yang diukur &mdash; dan berakhir dengan semakan yang kawasan pengesanannya sampai jauh ke bahagian dalam litar. Dalam contoh perkakasan di Bahagian 1 dan 2, kita menimbang keuntungan daripada pasca-pemilihan berbanding kosnya dalam gate tambahan dan shot yang dibuang.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This lesson is organized in two parts.\n"
msgstr "Pelajaran ini disusun dalam dua bahagian.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Part 1: End-of-circuit detection. All check information is read out at the end of the circuit. We consider two strategies under this constraint: in [Section 1.1](#symmetry-post-selection), the circuit is run unchanged and a known symmetry of the ideal output distribution serves as the check; in [Section 1.2](#stabilizer-code), additional gates are appended at the end of the circuit, and their measurement outcome serves as the check.\n"
msgstr "Bahagian 1: Pengesanan di hujung litar. Semua maklumat semakan dibaca di hujung litar. Kita mempertimbangkan dua strategi di bawah kekangan ini: dalam [Seksyen 1.1](#symmetry-post-selection), litar dijalankan tanpa perubahan dan simetri yang diketahui bagi taburan output unggul berfungsi sebagai semakan; dalam [Seksyen 1.2](#stabilizer-code), gate tambahan ditambah di hujung litar, dan hasil pengukurannya berfungsi sebagai semakan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Part 2: Mid-circuit detection. Check operations are sensitive to errors that occur during the circuit's execution, defining a detection region, the set of locations at which a fault would be flagged by the check. We develop two such methods: coherent Pauli checks, which use a paired check construction applicable to any Clifford circuit, and spacetime codes, which exploit the specific circuit's structure to reduce overhead.\n"
msgstr "Bahagian 2: Pengesanan pertengahan litar. Operasi semakan peka terhadap ralat yang berlaku semasa pelaksanaan litar, menentukan kawasan pengesanan, iaitu set lokasi di mana kerosakan akan ditandakan oleh semakan. Kita membangunkan dua kaedah sedemikian: semakan Pauli koheren, yang menggunakan binaan semakan berpasangan yang terpakai pada mana-mana litar Clifford, dan kod ruang-masa, yang memanfaatkan struktur litar tertentu untuk mengurangkan overhed.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Fault tolerance remains the north star. The first IBM fault-tolerant quantum computer, IBM Quantum&reg; Starling, is designed around quantum LDPC codes rather than the detection schemes practiced here, and IBM expects error mitigation and post-selection to keep working alongside error correction even then. The skills in this lesson, choosing what to check, placing checks where they catch the most, and accounting for their cost, carry over to that setting.\n"
msgstr "Toleransi kerosakan kekal sebagai bintang utara. Komputer kuantum toleran kerosakan pertama IBM, IBM Quantum&reg; Starling, direka berasaskan kod LDPC kuantum dan bukannya skema pengesanan yang diamalkan di sini, dan IBM menjangkakan mitigasi ralat dan pasca-pemilihan terus berfungsi bersama pembetulan ralat walaupun ketika itu. Kemahiran dalam pelajaran ini, iaitu memilih apa yang hendak disemak, meletakkan semakan di tempat ia menangkap paling banyak, dan mengambil kira kosnya, boleh dipindahkan ke tetapan tersebut.\n"

