# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Part 1: End-of-circuit detection {#part-1-end-of-circuit-detection}"
msgstr "Bahagian 1: Pengesanan di hujung litar {#part-1-end-of-circuit-detection}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In Part 1, we focus on methods in which all check information is read out at the end of the circuit. We consider two strategies under this constraint:\n"
msgstr "Dalam Bahagian 1, kita memberi tumpuan kepada kaedah yang semua maklumat semakannya dibaca di hujung litar. Kita mempertimbangkan dua strategi di bawah kekangan ini:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Symmetry post-selection: the simplest but most limited form ([Section 1.1](#symmetry-post-selection)). The check is a rule applied to the measured bitstring, and the original circuit is run unchanged, with no extra qubits, and no encoding. This requires prior knowledge of the ideal output distribution, and the data is consumed by the final measurement before the check is applied.\n"
msgstr "Pasca-pemilihan simetri: bentuk yang paling mudah tetapi paling terhad ([Seksyen 1.1](#symmetry-post-selection)). Semakannya ialah peraturan yang dikenakan pada rentetan bit yang diukur, dan litar asal dijalankan tanpa perubahan, tanpa qubit tambahan, dan tanpa pengekodan. Ini memerlukan pengetahuan terdahulu tentang taburan output unggul, dan data digunakan oleh pengukuran akhir sebelum semakan dikenakan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Stabilizer-code post-selection with syndrome qubits ([Section 1.2](#stabilizer-code)). The check is the outcome of an ancilla measurement appended to the circuit. This adds qubits and gates, but does not require knowing the full output distribution and can detect both bit-flip and phase-flip Pauli errors.\n"
msgstr "Pasca-pemilihan kod penstabil dengan qubit sindrom ([Seksyen 1.2](#stabilizer-code)). Semakannya ialah hasil pengukuran ancilla yang ditambah pada litar. Ini menambah qubit dan gate, tetapi tidak memerlukan pengetahuan tentang keseluruhan taburan output dan boleh mengesan ralat Pauli balik-bit dan balik-fasa.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Both strategies are post-selected: a flagged shot is discarded, and no correction is attempted. [Section 1.3](#limitations) outlines three limitations of end-of-circuit detection that motivate the interior-check constructions of Part 2.\n"
msgstr "Kedua-dua strategi ialah pasca-pilih: shot yang ditandakan dibuang, dan tiada pembetulan dicuba. [Seksyen 1.3](#limitations) menggariskan tiga had pengesanan di hujung litar yang mendorong binaan semakan dalaman pada Bahagian 2.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<Admonition type=\"note\" title=\"Prerequisite\">\n"
msgstr "<Admonition type=\"note\" title=\"Prasyarat\">\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This part assumes the stabilizer formalism at the level of the IBM Quantum Learning *Foundations of Quantum Error Correction* course, specifically [*Repetition code revisited*](/learning/courses/foundations-of-quantum-error-correction/stabilizer-formalism/repetition-code-revisited) and [*Stabilizer codes*](/learning/courses/foundations-of-quantum-error-correction/stabilizer-formalism/stabilizer-codes). Codespace, stabilizer generators, syndromes via anti-commutation, code distance, and $[[n,k,d]]$ notation are defined there. We include a short refresher before using these terms operationally in [Section 1.2](#stabilizer-code).\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
"<span id=\"symmetry-post-selection\"></span>\n"
msgstr ""
"Bahagian ini mengandaikan formalisme penstabil pada tahap kursus IBM Quantum Learning *Foundations of Quantum Error Correction*, khususnya [*Repetition code revisited*](/learning/courses/foundations-of-quantum-error-correction/stabilizer-formalism/repetition-code-revisited) dan [*Stabilizer codes*](/learning/courses/foundations-of-quantum-error-correction/stabilizer-formalism/stabilizer-codes). Ruang kod, penjana penstabil, sindrom melalui anti-kekommutan, jarak kod, dan tatatanda $[[n,k,d]]$ ditakrifkan di sana. Kami menyertakan penyegaran ringkas sebelum menggunakan istilah ini secara operasi dalam [Seksyen 1.2](#stabilizer-code).\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
"<span id=\"symmetry-post-selection\"></span>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "1.1 Symmetry post-selection on classical bitstrings {#11-symmetry-post-selection-on-classical-bitstrings}"
msgstr "1.1 Pasca-pemilihan simetri pada rentetan bit klasik {#11-symmetry-post-selection-on-classical-bitstrings}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Parity checking is a classical error-detection technique. The [parity](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Parity_bit) of a bitstring is the number of `1`s it contains, modulo 2. In the example below, a sender appends a parity bit to each data block so that the total number of `1`s in the resulting codeword is even.\n"
msgstr "Semakan pariti ialah teknik pengesanan ralat klasik. [Pariti](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Parity_bit) bagi sesuatu rentetan bit ialah bilangan `1` yang terkandung di dalamnya, modulo 2. Dalam contoh di bawah, penghantar menambah bit pariti pada setiap blok data supaya jumlah `1` dalam perkataan kod yang terhasil adalah genap.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Data (7 bits) | Number of 1s | Parity bit | Codeword with even parity (8 bits) |\n"
"|:---:|:---:|:---:|:---:|\n"
"| `0000000` | 0 | 0 | `00000000` |\n"
"| `1010001` | 3 | 1 | `10100011` |\n"
"| `1101001` | 4 | 0 | `11010010` |\n"
"| `1111111` | 7 | 1 | `11111111` |\n"
msgstr ""
"| Data (7 bit) | Bilangan 1 | Bit pariti | Perkataan kod dengan pariti genap (8 bit) |\n"
"|:---:|:---:|:---:|:---:|\n"
"| `0000000` | 0 | 0 | `00000000` |\n"
"| `1010001` | 3 | 1 | `10100011` |\n"
"| `1101001` | 4 | 0 | `11010010` |\n"
"| `1111111` | 7 | 1 | `11111111` |\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The receiver recomputes the parity of the 8-bit codeword and rejects it if the parity is no longer even. A single bit-flip during transmission changes the parity by one and is flagged; two flips leave the parity unchanged and slip through undetected.\n"
msgstr "Penerima mengira semula pariti perkataan kod 8 bit dan menolaknya jika pariti tidak lagi genap. Satu pembalikan bit semasa penghantaran mengubah pariti sebanyak satu dan akan ditandakan; dua pembalikan membiarkan pariti tidak berubah dan terlepas tanpa dikesan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The same idea, a structural rule on the bitstring that valid messages must satisfy, applies to the measurement outcomes of a quantum circuit. Parity is one such rule, but it is not the only one. More generally, when the ideal output distribution of a circuit is restricted by some structural constraint, that constraint can be used as the check: any measured bitstring that violates it can be rejected in classical post-processing as likely corrupted.\n"
msgstr "Idea yang sama, iaitu peraturan struktur pada rentetan bit yang mesti dipenuhi oleh mesej yang sah, terpakai pada hasil pengukuran bagi litar kuantum. Pariti ialah satu peraturan sedemikian, tetapi bukan satu-satunya. Secara lebih umum, apabila taburan output unggul sesuatu litar dihadkan oleh sesuatu kekangan struktur, kekangan itu boleh digunakan sebagai semakan: sebarang rentetan bit terukur yang melanggarnya boleh ditolak dalam pasca-pemprosesan klasik kerana berkemungkinan rosak.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Such constraints typically originate from a [*symmetry*](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Symmetry_in_quantum_mechanics) of the ideal state; in other words, an operator $S$ that leaves the state invariant ($S|\\psi\\rangle = |\\psi\\rangle$), so that measurement outcomes must respect the constraint associated with $S$. For example, the GHZ state $(|0^n\\rangle + |1^n\\rangle)/\\sqrt{2}$ is stabilized by the pairwise parity operators $Z_i Z_j$, which enforce the all-agree computational-basis support $\\{0^n, 1^n\\}$; it is also stabilized by $X^{\\otimes n}$, which fixes the relative $+$ phase between the two components. As another example, in an occupation-number encoding of an electronic-structure problem, particle-number conservation restricts measurement outcomes to a fixed sector, so outcomes outside that sector can be rejected in classical post-processing as unphysical. This is why the technique is commonly called *symmetry post-selection*. It requires no extra qubits, no encoding, and no syndrome extraction, and thus the original circuit is run unchanged.\n"
msgstr "Kekangan sebegini lazimnya berpunca daripada [*simetri*](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Symmetry_in_quantum_mechanics) keadaan unggul; dengan kata lain, pengendali $S$ yang membiarkan keadaan itu tidak berubah ($S|\\psi\\rangle = |\\psi\\rangle$), supaya hasil pengukuran mesti mematuhi kekangan yang berkaitan dengan $S$. Contohnya, keadaan GHZ $(|0^n\\rangle + |1^n\\rangle)/\\sqrt{2}$ distabilkan oleh pengendali pariti berpasangan $Z_i Z_j$, yang menguatkuasakan sokongan asas pengiraan semua-sepakat $\\{0^n, 1^n\\}$; ia juga distabilkan oleh $X^{\\otimes n}$, yang menetapkan fasa $+$ relatif antara kedua-dua komponen. Sebagai contoh lain, dalam pengekodan nombor-pendudukan bagi masalah struktur elektronik, pemuliharaan bilangan zarah menghadkan hasil pengukuran kepada sektor tetap, supaya hasil di luar sektor itu boleh ditolak dalam pasca-pemprosesan klasik sebagai tidak fizikal. Inilah sebabnya teknik ini lazim dipanggil *pasca-pemilihan simetri*. Ia tidak memerlukan qubit tambahan, pengekodan, atau pengekstrakan sindrom, maka litar asal dijalankan tanpa diubah.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The simplicity comes with two costs. First, the check operates entirely on the post-measurement record: errors that are visible in the bitstring can be flagged, but the quantum information itself is consumed by the final measurement before any check is applied, so the technique cannot protect a state for further use. Second, it requires that the ideal output distribution have a known structure that can be tested directly on a bitstring; for example, the two-bitstring support of a GHZ state, or a fixed particle-number sector of a chemistry ansatz. Most deep computational circuits do not come with such diagnostic structure, in which case no symmetry rule is available. The technique is best viewed as a low-overhead first line of defense for circuits whose ideal output is well understood, rather than a general-purpose detection method.\n"
msgstr "Kesederhanaan ini datang dengan dua kos. Pertama, semakan beroperasi sepenuhnya pada rekod selepas pengukuran: ralat yang kelihatan dalam rentetan bit boleh ditandakan, tetapi maklumat kuantum itu sendiri telah digunakan oleh pengukuran akhir sebelum sebarang semakan dibuat, justeru teknik ini tidak dapat melindungi keadaan untuk kegunaan selanjutnya. Kedua, ia memerlukan taburan output unggul mempunyai struktur diketahui yang boleh diuji terus pada rentetan bit; contohnya, sokongan dua rentetan bit bagi keadaan GHZ, atau sektor bilangan zarah tetap bagi ansatz kimia. Kebanyakan litar pengiraan yang dalam tidak mempunyai struktur diagnostik sebegini, dan dalam hal itu tiada peraturan simetri tersedia. Teknik ini paling baik dilihat sebagai barisan pertahanan pertama berkos rendah bagi litar yang output uggulnya difahami dengan baik, dan bukannya kaedah pengesanan serba guna.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Even so, symmetry post-selection is an instructive entry point: it is simple enough to expose the core trade-offs of post-selected detection (post-selection rate, sampling overhead, and fidelity) that recur throughout the rest of the notebook. We define these quantities next.\n"
msgstr "Walaupun begitu, pasca-pemilihan simetri ialah titik permulaan yang bermanfaat: ia cukup mudah untuk mendedahkan pertukaran utama dalam pengesanan berpasca-pemilihan (kadar pasca-pemilihan, overhed pensampelan dan kesetiaan) yang berulang sepanjang buku nota ini. Kita takrifkan kuantiti ini seterusnya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Definitions {#definitions}"
msgstr "Takrifan {#definitions}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We use the following terms throughout the notebook.\n"
msgstr "Kita menggunakan istilah berikut sepanjang buku nota ini.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "*Post-selection rate* $A$ (also called *acceptance rate*): the fraction of shots that satisfy the check.\n"
msgstr "*Kadar pasca-pemilihan* $A$ (juga dipanggil *kadar penerimaan*): pecahan syot yang memenuhi semakan.\n"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "*Sampling overhead* $1/A$: the multiplicative factor by which raw shots must grow to recover one accepted shot.\n"
msgstr "*Overhed pensampelan* $1/A$: faktor darab yang perlu digandakan pada bilangan syot mentah untuk mendapatkan satu syot yang diterima.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "[*Hellinger fidelity*](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/quantum_info#hellinger_fidelity) between two probability distributions $p$ and $q$ on $n$-bit strings:\n"
msgstr "[*Kesetiaan Hellinger*](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/quantum_info#hellinger_fidelity) antara dua taburan kebarangkalian $p$ dan $q$ pada rentetan $n$-bit:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "    $$F(p, q) = \\bigg(\\sum_i \\sqrt{p_i\\, q_i}\\,\\bigg)^2,$$\n"
msgstr "    $$F(p, q) = \\bigg(\\sum_i \\sqrt{p_i\\, q_i}\\,\\bigg)^2,$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  where the sum runs over all $n$-bit strings $i$, and $p_i$ and $q_i$ are the probabilities that $p$ and $q$ assign to $i$. $F = 1$ for identical distributions and $F = 0$ when no bitstring is assigned positive probability by both distributions. $F$ is a classical distribution-level quantity computed *after* measurement and does not certify the full quantum state; for example, a GHZ state and its phase-flipped counterpart can produce identical computational-basis distributions and therefore identical $F$. We return to this potential obstacle when motivating stabilizer-code checks in [Section 1.2](#stabilizer-code).\n"
"- *Detection region* of a check: the set of circuit locations at which a fault can flip that check; which Pauli types are caught at each location depends on the check. The final checks of Part 1 can only respond to faults whose effects survive to the final measurements, and whether a surviving fault is actually detected depends on the particular check. Part 2 places checks whose regions are deliberately narrower and traces them through the circuit.\n"
msgstr ""
"  dengan hasil tambah merentasi semua rentetan $n$-bit $i$, dan $p_i$ serta $q_i$ ialah kebarangkalian yang diberikan oleh $p$ dan $q$ kepada $i$. $F = 1$ bagi taburan yang serupa dan $F = 0$ apabila tiada rentetan bit diberi kebarangkalian positif oleh kedua-dua taburan. $F$ ialah kuantiti klasik peringkat taburan yang dikira *selepas* pengukuran dan tidak mengesahkan keseluruhan keadaan kuantum; contohnya, keadaan GHZ dan pasangannya yang dibalikkan fasa boleh menghasilkan taburan asas pengiraan yang serupa dan oleh itu $F$ yang serupa. Kita kembali kepada halangan berpotensi ini apabila memotivasikan semakan kod penstabil dalam [Bahagian 1.2](#stabilizer-code).\n"
"- *Rantau pengesanan* bagi sesuatu semakan: set lokasi litar di mana ralat boleh membalikkan semakan itu; jenis Pauli yang ditangkap di setiap lokasi bergantung pada semakan tersebut. Semakan akhir Bahagian 1 hanya boleh bertindak balas terhadap ralat yang kesannya kekal hingga pengukuran akhir, dan sama ada ralat yang kekal itu benar-benar dikesan bergantung pada semakan tertentu. Bahagian 2 menempatkan semakan yang rantaunya sengaja lebih sempit dan menjejakinya melalui litar.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "1.1.1 GHZ as a benchmark for symmetry filtering {#111-ghz-as-a-benchmark-for-symmetry-filtering}"
msgstr "1.1.1 GHZ sebagai penanda aras untuk penapisan simetri {#111-ghz-as-a-benchmark-for-symmetry-filtering}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We use the $n$-qubit GHZ state\n"
"$$\n"
"|\\mathrm{GHZ}_n\\rangle = \\tfrac{1}{\\sqrt 2}\\big(|0\\rangle^{\\otimes n} + |1\\rangle^{\\otimes n}\\big).\n"
"$$\n"
"In the computational basis, the ideal outcome distribution is supported on exactly two bitstrings, $0^n$ and $1^n$. Any other bitstring can be rejected in classical post-processing as inconsistent with this support.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita menggunakan keadaan GHZ $n$-qubit\n"
"$$\n"
"|\\mathrm{GHZ}_n\\rangle = \\tfrac{1}{\\sqrt 2}\\big(|0\\rangle^{\\otimes n} + |1\\rangle^{\\otimes n}\\big).\n"
"$$\n"
"Dalam asas pengiraan, taburan hasil unggul disokong pada tepat dua rentetan bit, $0^n$ dan $1^n$. Sebarang rentetan bit lain boleh ditolak dalam pasca-pemprosesan klasik kerana tidak konsisten dengan sokongan ini.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For our run we use $n = 10$. Both ideal outputs $0^{10}$ and $1^{10}$ have an even number of `1`s (0 and 10, respectively), so we compare two rules on the same dataset:\n"
msgstr "Untuk larian kita, kita menggunakan $n = 10$. Kedua-dua output unggul $0^{10}$ dan $1^{10}$ mempunyai bilangan `1` yang genap (masing-masing 0 dan 10), jadi kita membandingkan dua peraturan pada set data yang sama:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "*Even-parity rule.* Keep shots whose number of `1`s is even. This rule applies only when $n$ is even (the case here); for odd $n$ the two ideal outputs have opposite parity, and no single parity rule keeps both.\n"
msgstr "*Peraturan pariti genap.* Simpan syot yang bilangan `1`-nya genap. Peraturan ini hanya terpakai apabila $n$ genap (seperti dalam kes ini); bagi $n$ ganjil, kedua-dua output unggul mempunyai pariti bertentangan, dan tiada satu peraturan pariti yang mengekalkan kedua-duanya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "*All-agree rule.* Keep shots that are exactly $0^n$ or $1^n$.\n"
msgstr "*Peraturan semua-sepakat.* Simpan syot yang tepat $0^n$ atau $1^n$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The all-agree rule is more restrictive than even parity: every all-agree bitstring has an even number of `1`s, but most bitstrings with an even number of `1`s are not all-agree. Even parity catches any odd number of bit flips but lets through any pair of compensating flips. Under noise, we therefore expect the all-agree rule to give higher post-selected fidelity at a lower post-selection rate.\n"
msgstr "Peraturan semua-sepakat lebih ketat daripada pariti genap: setiap rentetan bit semua-sepakat mempunyai bilangan `1` yang genap, tetapi kebanyakan rentetan bit dengan bilangan `1` genap bukan semua-sepakat. Pariti genap menangkap sebarang bilangan pembalikan bit yang ganjil tetapi membiarkan lepas sebarang pasangan pembalikan yang saling mengimbangi. Di bawah hingar, kita oleh itu menjangkakan peraturan semua-sepakat memberikan kesetiaan pasca-pemilihan yang lebih tinggi pada kadar pasca-pemilihan yang lebih rendah.\n"

