msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/tools-for-quantum-advantage/error-correction-i/extracted-outputs/a8a2a77c-0.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Run the 10-qubit GHZ circuit on the hardware backend.\n"
msgstr "Jalankan litar GHZ 10-qubit pada backend perkakasan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Apply both rules to the same dataset.\n"
msgstr "Gunakan kedua-dua peraturan pada set data yang sama.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/tools-for-quantum-advantage/error-correction-i/extracted-outputs/2a7ded50-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/tools-for-quantum-advantage/error-correction-i/extracted-outputs/2a7ded50-0.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Use the plot to compare the Hellinger fidelity and acceptance of the two filters. The all-agree rule keeps a subset of the even-parity shots, so its acceptance cannot be higher. This is the accuracy-throughput trade-off introduced by post-selection: stricter filters can make the accepted distribution cleaner, but they also reduce the number of usable samples and therefore raise the sampling overhead. Here both filters preserve the full ideal GHZ support, so Hellinger fidelity cannot decrease as the accepted set shrinks, provided some shots remain. Every shot the all-agree rule keeps lies in the ideal support by construction, so its Hellinger fidelity falls short of 1 only when $0^n$ and $1^n$ are not equally frequent. This distribution-level improvement does not certify phase coherence.\n"
msgstr "Gunakan plot untuk membandingkan kesetiaan Hellinger dan kadar penerimaan kedua-dua penapis. Peraturan semua-sepakat mengekalkan subset syot pariti genap, maka penerimaannya tidak boleh lebih tinggi. Inilah pertukaran ketepatan-daya pemprosesan yang diperkenalkan oleh pasca-pemilihan: penapis yang lebih ketat boleh menjadikan taburan yang diterima lebih bersih, tetapi ia juga mengurangkan bilangan sampel yang boleh digunakan dan seterusnya meningkatkan overhed pensampelan. Di sini kedua-dua penapis mengekalkan keseluruhan sokongan GHZ unggul, jadi kesetiaan Hellinger tidak boleh berkurang apabila set yang diterima mengecil, dengan syarat beberapa syot masih ada. Setiap syot yang dikekalkan oleh peraturan semua-sepakat berada dalam sokongan unggul secara pembinaan, jadi kesetiaan Hellingernya kurang daripada 1 hanya apabila $0^n$ dan $1^n$ tidak sama kekerapan. Peningkatan peringkat taburan ini tidak mengesahkan koheren fasa.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Even parity is good at catching any odd number of bit flips, but it has a structural flaw: any pair of compensating flips slips through. The next subsection addresses this issue.\n"
"<span id=\"parity\"></span>\n"
msgstr ""
"Pariti genap bagus dalam menangkap sebarang bilangan pembalikan bit yang ganjil, tetapi ia mempunyai kelemahan struktur: sebarang pasangan pembalikan yang saling mengimbangi terlepas. Subseksyen seterusnya menangani isu ini.\n"
"<span id=\"parity\"></span>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "1.1.2 When parity is not enough {#112-when-parity-is-not-enough}"
msgstr "1.1.2 Apabila pariti tidak mencukupi {#112-when-parity-is-not-enough}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Even parity catches any odd number of bit flips but lets through any even number of flips. We can quantify this directly from the hardware run above: every shot that satisfies the even-parity rule but is *not* in the all-agree set $\\{0^{10}, 1^{10}\\}$ is a corrupted shot that an even number of bit flips moved into the same parity sector as the ideal output.\n"
msgstr "Pariti genap menangkap sebarang bilangan pembalikan bit yang ganjil tetapi membiarkan lepas sebarang bilangan pembalikan yang genap. Kita boleh mengukur perkara ini secara langsung daripada larian perkakasan di atas: setiap syot yang memenuhi peraturan pariti genap tetapi *tidak* berada dalam set semua-sepakat $\\{0^{10}, 1^{10}\\}$ ialah syot rosak yang telah dialihkan oleh bilangan pembalikan bit yang genap ke dalam sektor pariti yang sama dengan output unggul.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The false-accept rate measures how often the even-parity rule accepts an output outside the ideal support.\n"
msgstr "Kadar terima-palsu mengukur kekerapan peraturan pariti genap menerima output di luar sokongan unggul.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The previous analysis exposes a more fundamental limitation: a final computational-basis filter only sees what is recorded in the bit values. Errors that change bit values (bit-flip errors) leave a trace there and can in principle be filtered. Errors that change only the *phase* between basis states (phase-flip errors) can rotate the relative phase between, say, $|0^n\\rangle$ and $|1^n\\rangle$ without changing the bitstring distribution, so no rule applied only to the final bitstrings can detect them.\n"
msgstr "Analisis sebelumnya mendedahkan had yang lebih asas: penapis asas pengiraan akhir hanya melihat apa yang direkodkan dalam nilai bit. Ralat yang mengubah nilai bit (ralat pembalikan bit) meninggalkan kesan di situ dan pada dasarnya boleh ditapis. Ralat yang hanya mengubah *fasa* antara keadaan asas (ralat pembalikan fasa) boleh memutarkan fasa relatif antara, katakan, $|0^n\\rangle$ dan $|1^n\\rangle$ tanpa mengubah taburan rentetan bit, maka tiada peraturan yang dikenakan hanya pada rentetan bit akhir dapat mengesannya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This limitation motivates the next section. To detect phase-flip errors, the check itself must access information that is not visible in the bitstring, which is what stabilizer codes provide.\n"
msgstr "Had ini memotivasikan bahagian seterusnya. Untuk mengesan ralat pembalikan fasa, semakan itu sendiri mesti mencapai maklumat yang tidak kelihatan dalam rentetan bit, dan inilah yang disediakan oleh kod penstabil.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Check your understanding {#check-your-understanding}"
msgstr "Semak kefahaman anda {#check-your-understanding}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Suppose you prepare a three-qubit state whose ideal outcomes are only `000` and `111`. What rule would you use for post-selection, and what single-qubit errors would that rule catch?\n"
msgstr "Andaikan anda menyediakan keadaan tiga qubit yang hasil uggulnya hanyalah `000` dan `111`. Apakah peraturan yang akan anda gunakan untuk pasca-pemilihan, dan apakah ralat qubit tunggal yang akan ditangkap oleh peraturan itu?\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Answer\">\n"
msgstr ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Jawapan\">\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The natural choice is the *all-agree rule*: keep only `000` and `111`. The even-parity rule does not work here, because `000` has zero $1$s and `111` has three, so their parities are opposite. Any single bit-flip ($X$) error breaks the all-agree pattern, so the rule catches every weight-$1$ bit-flip. It does *not* catch phase-flip ($Z$) errors, which leave bit values unchanged. The phase-flip problem motivates [Section 1.2](#stabilizer-code).\n"
msgstr "Pilihan yang wajar ialah *peraturan semua-sepakat*: simpan hanya `000` dan `111`. Peraturan pariti genap tidak berfungsi di sini, kerana `000` mempunyai sifar $1$ dan `111` mempunyai tiga, maka pariti mereka bertentangan. Sebarang ralat pembalikan bit ($X$) tunggal memecahkan corak semua-sepakat, jadi peraturan ini menangkap setiap pembalikan bit berpemberat-$1$. Ia *tidak* menangkap ralat pembalikan fasa ($Z$), yang membiarkan nilai bit tidak berubah. Masalah pembalikan fasa ini memotivasikan [Bahagian 1.2](#stabilizer-code).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"</Accordion>\n"
"<span id=\"stabilizer-code\"></span>\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "1.2 Stabilizer-code post-selection: the $[[4,2,2]]$ code {#12-stabilizer-code-post-selection-the-422-code}"
msgstr "1.2 Pasca-pemilihan kod penstabil: kod $[[4,2,2]]$ {#12-stabilizer-code-post-selection-the-422-code}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "[Section 1.1](#symmetry-post-selection) left two open limitations. First, the bitstring rules used there only see what is recorded in the [computational basis](/learning/courses/basics-of-quantum-information/multiple-systems/quantum-information#measurements-of-quantum-states), that is, the eigenbasis of the $Z$ operator. They cannot see phase-flip errors, which are invisible in that basis. (Changing the measurement basis can make different error information visible, but no single final measurement basis gives a complete, non-destructive check of both bit- and phase-type errors for an arbitrary encoded state.) Second, applying the check requires measuring the data qubits, which collapses the state and consumes the information we wanted to keep. The classical fix to the second problem, keeping redundant copies and checking that they agree, is unavailable here because the [no-cloning theorem](/learning/courses/basics-of-quantum-information/quantum-circuits/limitations-on-quantum-information#no-cloning-theorem) forbids duplicating an unknown quantum state.\n"
msgstr "[Bahagian 1.1](#symmetry-post-selection) meninggalkan dua had yang belum selesai. Pertama, peraturan rentetan bit yang digunakan di sana hanya melihat apa yang direkodkan dalam [asas pengiraan](/learning/courses/basics-of-quantum-information/multiple-systems/quantum-information#measurements-of-quantum-states), iaitu asas eigen bagi pengendali $Z$. Ia tidak dapat melihat ralat pembalikan fasa, yang tidak kelihatan dalam asas itu. (Menukar asas pengukuran boleh menjadikan maklumat ralat yang berbeza kelihatan, tetapi tiada satu asas pengukuran akhir yang memberikan semakan lengkap dan tidak merosakkan bagi ralat jenis bit dan jenis fasa untuk keadaan terkod yang sewenang-wenang.) Kedua, melaksanakan semakan memerlukan pengukuran qubit data, yang meruntuhkan keadaan dan menggunakan maklumat yang ingin kita kekalkan. Penyelesaian klasik bagi masalah kedua, iaitu menyimpan salinan berlebihan dan menyemak bahawa ia sepadan, tidak tersedia di sini kerana [teorem tanpa-pengklonan](/learning/courses/basics-of-quantum-information/quantum-circuits/limitations-on-quantum-information#no-cloning-theorem) melarang penggandaan keadaan kuantum yang tidak diketahui.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Why no-cloning matters here\">\n"
msgstr ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Mengapa tanpa-pengklonan penting di sini\">\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The [no-cloning theorem](/learning/courses/basics-of-quantum-information/quantum-circuits/limitations-on-quantum-information#no-cloning-theorem) says there is no unitary $U$ that takes an arbitrary unknown state $|\\psi\\rangle$ together with a fresh register and produces $|\\psi\\rangle \\otimes |\\psi\\rangle$. Cloning is a *non-linear* operation in $|\\psi\\rangle$, but every quantum operation is linear: if $U$ cloned the two basis states $|0\\rangle$ and $|1\\rangle$, linearity would force $U$ to send the superposition $\\tfrac{1}{\\sqrt 2}(|0\\rangle+|1\\rangle)$ to $\\tfrac{1}{\\sqrt 2}(|0\\rangle|0\\rangle+|1\\rangle|1\\rangle)$, which is *not* the cloned state $\\tfrac{1}{\\sqrt 2}(|0\\rangle+|1\\rangle) \\otimes \\tfrac{1}{\\sqrt 2}(|0\\rangle+|1\\rangle)$. The contradiction arises specifically because the input is a superposition; cloning basis states alone is fine.\n"
msgstr "[Teorem tanpa-pengklonan](/learning/courses/basics-of-quantum-information/quantum-circuits/limitations-on-quantum-information#no-cloning-theorem) menyatakan bahawa tiada unitari $U$ yang mengambil keadaan tidak diketahui yang sewenang-wenang $|\\psi\\rangle$ bersama daftar baharu dan menghasilkan $|\\psi\\rangle \\otimes |\\psi\\rangle$. Pengklonan ialah operasi *tak linear* dalam $|\\psi\\rangle$, tetapi setiap operasi kuantum adalah linear: jika $U$ mengklon dua keadaan asas $|0\\rangle$ dan $|1\\rangle$, kelinearan akan memaksa $U$ menghantar superposisi $\\tfrac{1}{\\sqrt 2}(|0\\rangle+|1\\rangle)$ kepada $\\tfrac{1}{\\sqrt 2}(|0\\rangle|0\\rangle+|1\\rangle|1\\rangle)$, yang *bukan* keadaan terklon $\\tfrac{1}{\\sqrt 2}(|0\\rangle+|1\\rangle) \\otimes \\tfrac{1}{\\sqrt 2}(|0\\rangle+|1\\rangle)$. Percanggahan ini timbul secara khusus kerana input ialah superposisi; mengklon keadaan asas sahaja tidak mengapa.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This does not forbid preparing multiple copies of a state we *already know how to prepare*: we can simply run the preparation procedure on fresh registers. A CNOT cleanly copies computational-basis information, sending $|a\\rangle|0\\rangle \\mapsto |a\\rangle|a\\rangle$ for $a \\in \\{0, 1\\}$, but this does not extend to arbitrary superpositions. The encoding circuits used by stabilizer codes combine the logical input, which may be unknown, with initialized ancillas and distribute its information across an encoded register without making copies. What no-cloning rules out is duplicating a state that arrives unknown from an earlier computation.\n"
msgstr "Ini tidak melarang penyediaan pelbagai salinan keadaan yang kita *sudah tahu cara menyediakannya*: kita hanya perlu menjalankan prosedur penyediaan pada daftar baharu. CNOT menyalin maklumat asas pengiraan dengan bersih, menghantar $|a\\rangle|0\\rangle \\mapsto |a\\rangle|a\\rangle$ bagi $a \\in \\{0, 1\\}$, tetapi ini tidak meluas kepada superposisi sewenang-wenang. Litar pengekodan yang digunakan oleh kod penstabil menggabungkan input logik, yang mungkin tidak diketahui, dengan ancilla yang dimulakan dan mengedarkan maklumatnya merentasi daftar terkod tanpa membuat salinan. Apa yang dilarang oleh tanpa-pengklonan ialah menggandakan keadaan yang tiba tanpa diketahui daripada pengiraan terdahulu.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"</Accordion>\n"
"Stabilizer codes resolve both limitations at once. The [logical state](/learning/courses/foundations-of-quantum-error-correction/stabilizer-formalism/repetition-code-revisited#syndromes) is encoded across multiple physical qubits through entanglement, and an ancilla qubit couples to the data to report a stabilizer eigenvalue, enough to flag whether the state has left the [codespace](/learning/courses/foundations-of-quantum-error-correction/stabilizer-formalism/stabilizer-codes), but not enough to reveal the logical amplitudes. By using two complementary stabilizers, one diagonal in the $Z$ basis and one in the $X$ basis, the check is sensitive to both bit-flip and phase-flip errors. Because only the ancilla is measured, this can in principle be applied without collapsing the encoded state. Used this way, the code is post-selected quantum error correction in its original form: an error-detecting code whose flagged shots are discarded rather than corrected. The reach of the check is bounded by the *code distance* $d$: with $d=2$, the $[[4,2,2]]$ code we use here detects every weight-$1$ Pauli error on a data qubit but is blind to certain weight-$2$ errors, including the even-bit-flip patterns that already escaped the parity rule in [Section 1.1.2](#parity).\n"
msgstr ""
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"</Accordion>\n"
"Kod penstabil menyelesaikan kedua-dua had sekaligus. [Keadaan logik](/learning/courses/foundations-of-quantum-error-correction/stabilizer-formalism/repetition-code-revisited#syndromes) dikodkan merentasi beberapa qubit fizikal melalui keterjeratan, dan qubit ancilla bergandingan dengan data untuk melaporkan nilai eigen penstabil, mencukupi untuk menandakan sama ada keadaan telah meninggalkan [ruang kod](/learning/courses/foundations-of-quantum-error-correction/stabilizer-formalism/stabilizer-codes), tetapi tidak mencukupi untuk mendedahkan amplitud logik. Dengan menggunakan dua penstabil pelengkap, satu pepenjuru dalam asas $Z$ dan satu dalam asas $X$, semakan ini peka terhadap ralat pembalikan bit dan pembalikan fasa. Oleh kerana hanya ancilla diukur, ini pada dasarnya boleh dilaksanakan tanpa meruntuhkan keadaan terkod. Apabila digunakan sedemikian, kod ini ialah pembetulan ralat kuantum berpasca-pemilihan dalam bentuk asalnya: kod pengesan ralat yang syot bertandanya dibuang dan bukannya dibetulkan. Jangkauan semakan dihadkan oleh *jarak kod* $d$: dengan $d=2$, kod $[[4,2,2]]$ yang kita gunakan di sini mengesan setiap ralat Pauli berpemberat-$1$ pada qubit data tetapi buta terhadap ralat berpemberat-$2$ tertentu, termasuk corak pembalikan bit genap yang sudah terlepas daripada peraturan pariti dalam [Bahagian 1.1.2](#parity).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Quick refresher on stabilizer-code terminology\">\n"
msgstr ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Ulang kaji pantas istilah kod penstabil\">\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The terms collected below are the ones used most often in this section. For full details, refer to the IBM Quantum Learning [*Stabilizer codes*](/learning/courses/foundations-of-quantum-error-correction/stabilizer-formalism/stabilizer-codes) course.\n"
msgstr "Istilah yang dihimpunkan di bawah ialah yang paling kerap digunakan dalam bahagian ini. Untuk butiran penuh, rujuk kursus IBM Quantum Learning [*Kod penstabil*](/learning/courses/foundations-of-quantum-error-correction/stabilizer-formalism/stabilizer-codes).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "*Physical qubit, logical qubit.* The hardware qubits used to store encoded information are the physical qubits. The abstract qubits whose state is being protected are the logical qubits.\n"
msgstr "*Qubit fizikal, qubit logik.* Qubit perkakasan yang digunakan untuk menyimpan maklumat terkod ialah qubit fizikal. Qubit abstrak yang keadaannya dilindungi ialah qubit logik.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "*Stabilizer generators.* A set of mutually commuting multi-qubit Pauli operators $P_1, \\ldots, P_r$. The states satisfying $P_k|\\psi\\rangle = |\\psi\\rangle$ for every $k$ form the codespace.\n"
msgstr "*Penjana penstabil.* Set pengendali Pauli berbilang qubit yang saling kalis tukar tertib $P_1, \\ldots, P_r$. Keadaan yang memenuhi $P_k|\\psi\\rangle = |\\psi\\rangle$ bagi setiap $k$ membentuk ruang kod.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "*Codespace.* The simultaneous $+1$ eigenspace of the stabilizer generators.\n"
msgstr "*Ruang kod.* Ruang eigen $+1$ serentak bagi penjana penstabil.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "*Ancilla qubit.* An auxiliary qubit coupled to the data qubits to extract a stabilizer eigenvalue without measuring the data directly.\n"
msgstr "*Qubit ancilla.* Qubit tambahan yang digandingkan dengan qubit data untuk mengekstrak nilai eigen penstabil tanpa mengukur data secara langsung.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "*Syndrome.* The string of stabilizer-measurement outcomes, under the convention that outcome `0` corresponds to eigenvalue $+1$ and outcome `1` to eigenvalue $-1$.\n"
msgstr "*Sindrom.* Rentetan hasil pengukuran penstabil, mengikut konvensyen bahawa hasil `0` sepadan dengan nilai eigen $+1$ dan hasil `1` dengan nilai eigen $-1$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "*$[[n, k, d]]$ notation.* A stabilizer code on $n$ physical qubits that encodes $k$ logical qubits with code distance $d$.\n"
msgstr "*Tatatanda $[[n, k, d]]$.* Kod penstabil pada $n$ qubit fizikal yang mengekod $k$ qubit logik dengan jarak kod $d$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "*Weight of a Pauli operator.* The number of qubits on which the operator acts as something other than the identity.\n"
msgstr "*Pemberat pengendali Pauli.* Bilangan qubit yang pengendali itu bertindak sebagai sesuatu selain identiti.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "*Logical operator.* A Pauli operator that commutes with every stabilizer generator and is not proportional to a stabilizer element.\n"
msgstr "*Pengendali logik.* Pengendali Pauli yang kalis tukar tertib dengan setiap penjana penstabil dan tidak berkadaran dengan unsur penstabil.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "*Code distance $d$.* The minimum weight of a logical operator.\n"
msgstr "*Jarak kod $d$.* Pemberat minimum bagi pengendali logik.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"</Accordion>\n"
"The $[[4,2,2]]$ code uses $n=4$ physical qubits to encode $k=2$ logical qubits with code distance $d=2$. Its codespace is the simultaneous $+1$ eigenspace of two stabilizer generators,\n"
"$$\n"
"Z_3 Z_2 Z_1 Z_0 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad X_3 X_2 X_1 X_0.\n"
"$$\n"
"A single-qubit $X$ error anti-commutes with $Z_3 Z_2 Z_1 Z_0$ and is flagged by the corresponding syndrome bit; a single-qubit $Z$ error anti-commutes with $X_3 X_2 X_1 X_0$ and is flagged by the other. Every weight-$1$ Pauli error on a data qubit is detected by at least one of the two stabilizers. The two-bit syndrome identifies the error type ($X$, $Z$, $Y$, or none) but not the qubit on which the error occurred. With $d=2$, this information is insufficient to determine a correction, so the $[[4,2,2]]$ code is used as a detection-only code.\n"
msgstr ""
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"</Accordion>\n"
"Kod $[[4,2,2]]$ menggunakan $n=4$ qubit fizikal untuk mengekod $k=2$ qubit logik dengan jarak kod $d=2$. Ruang kodnya ialah ruang eigen $+1$ serentak bagi dua penjana penstabil,\n"
"$$\n"
"Z_3 Z_2 Z_1 Z_0 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad X_3 X_2 X_1 X_0.\n"
"$$\n"
"Ralat $X$ qubit tunggal anti-kalis tukar tertib dengan $Z_3 Z_2 Z_1 Z_0$ dan ditandakan oleh bit sindrom yang sepadan; ralat $Z$ qubit tunggal anti-kalis tukar tertib dengan $X_3 X_2 X_1 X_0$ dan ditandakan oleh yang satu lagi. Setiap ralat Pauli berpemberat-$1$ pada qubit data dikesan oleh sekurang-kurangnya satu daripada dua penstabil. Sindrom dua bit mengenal pasti jenis ralat ($X$, $Z$, $Y$, atau tiada) tetapi bukan qubit tempat ralat itu berlaku. Dengan $d=2$, maklumat ini tidak mencukupi untuk menentukan pembetulan, maka kod $[[4,2,2]]$ digunakan sebagai kod pengesanan sahaja.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The experiments below run syndrome extraction on the logical Bell state:\n"
"$$\n"
"|\\Phi^+\\rangle_L = \\tfrac{1}{\\sqrt 2}\\big(|00\\rangle_L + |11\\rangle_L\\big),\n"
"$$\n"
"a state in the codespace.\n"
msgstr ""
"Eksperimen di bawah menjalankan pengekstrakan sindrom pada keadaan Bell logik:\n"
"$$\n"
"|\\Phi^+\\rangle_L = \\tfrac{1}{\\sqrt 2}\\big(|00\\rangle_L + |11\\rangle_L\\big),\n"
"$$\n"
"suatu keadaan dalam ruang kod.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Logical basis states of the [[4,2,2]] code\">\n"
msgstr ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Keadaan asas logik bagi kod [[4,2,2]]\">\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The $[[4,2,2]]$ code encodes two logical qubits using four physical qubits. As with any two-qubit system, there are four logical computational-basis states, $|00\\rangle_L$, $|01\\rangle_L$, $|10\\rangle_L$, $|11\\rangle_L$, read as the values of the two encoded qubits (for example, $|00\\rangle_L$ has both logical qubits in the logical-zero state). What makes this an *encoding* is that each $|ab\\rangle_L$ is a specific superposition of physical four-qubit basis states, chosen so that all four logical basis states satisfy the codespace conditions $Z_3 Z_2 Z_1 Z_0 = +1$ and $X_3 X_2 X_1 X_0 = +1$.\n"
msgstr "Kod $[[4,2,2]]$ mengekod dua qubit logik menggunakan empat qubit fizikal. Seperti mana-mana sistem dua qubit, terdapat empat keadaan asas pengiraan logik, $|00\\rangle_L$, $|01\\rangle_L$, $|10\\rangle_L$, $|11\\rangle_L$, dibaca sebagai nilai dua qubit terkod (contohnya, $|00\\rangle_L$ mempunyai kedua-dua qubit logik dalam keadaan sifar-logik). Apa yang menjadikannya satu *pengekodan* ialah setiap $|ab\\rangle_L$ merupakan superposisi tertentu keadaan asas empat qubit fizikal, dipilih supaya keempat-empat keadaan asas logik memenuhi syarat ruang kod $Z_3 Z_2 Z_1 Z_0 = +1$ dan $X_3 X_2 X_1 X_0 = +1$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The standard choice is\n"
msgstr "Pilihan piawai ialah\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"|00\\rangle_L &= \\tfrac{1}{\\sqrt 2}\\big(|0000\\rangle + |1111\\rangle\\big), \\\\\n"
"|01\\rangle_L &= \\tfrac{1}{\\sqrt 2}\\big(|0011\\rangle + |1100\\rangle\\big), \\\\\n"
"|10\\rangle_L &= \\tfrac{1}{\\sqrt 2}\\big(|0101\\rangle + |1010\\rangle\\big), \\\\\n"
"|11\\rangle_L &= \\tfrac{1}{\\sqrt 2}\\big(|0110\\rangle + |1001\\rangle\\big).\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"|00\\rangle_L &= \\tfrac{1}{\\sqrt 2}\\big(|0000\\rangle + |1111\\rangle\\big), \\\\\n"
"|01\\rangle_L &= \\tfrac{1}{\\sqrt 2}\\big(|0011\\rangle + |1100\\rangle\\big), \\\\\n"
"|10\\rangle_L &= \\tfrac{1}{\\sqrt 2}\\big(|0101\\rangle + |1010\\rangle\\big), \\\\\n"
"|11\\rangle_L &= \\tfrac{1}{\\sqrt 2}\\big(|0110\\rangle + |1001\\rangle\\big).\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Each line pairs two four-qubit strings related by flipping all four bits. Both strings in each line have an even number of $1$s. Since $Z$ has eigenvalue $+1$ on $|0\\rangle$ and $-1$ on $|1\\rangle$, the eigenvalue of $Z_3 Z_2 Z_1 Z_0$ on a computational-basis string is $(-1)^{\\text{number of }1\\text{s}}$, so a string with an even number of $1$s gives eigenvalue $+1$. The $+$ combination is also invariant under $X_3 X_2 X_1 X_0$, which simply permutes the two terms within each line.\n"
msgstr "Setiap baris memadankan dua rentetan empat qubit yang berkait melalui pembalikan keempat-empat bit. Kedua-dua rentetan dalam setiap baris mempunyai bilangan $1$ yang genap. Oleh kerana $Z$ mempunyai nilai eigen $+1$ pada $|0\\rangle$ dan $-1$ pada $|1\\rangle$, nilai eigen $Z_3 Z_2 Z_1 Z_0$ pada rentetan asas pengiraan ialah $(-1)^{\\text{number of }1\\text{s}}$, maka rentetan dengan bilangan $1$ genap memberikan nilai eigen $+1$. Gabungan $+$ juga tidak berubah di bawah $X_3 X_2 X_1 X_0$, yang hanya menukar tertib kedua-dua sebutan dalam setiap baris.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The logical Bell state used in the experiments is:\n"
"$$\n"
"|\\Phi^+\\rangle_L = \\tfrac{1}{\\sqrt 2}\\big(|00\\rangle_L + |11\\rangle_L\\big),\n"
"$$\n"
"the analog of the standard Bell state $\\tfrac{1}{\\sqrt 2}(|00\\rangle + |11\\rangle)$ on the two logical qubits. Substituting the codeword expressions above gives its physical four-qubit form:\n"
"$$\n"
"|\\Phi^+\\rangle_L = \\tfrac{1}{2}\\big(|0000\\rangle + |1111\\rangle + |0110\\rangle + |1001\\rangle\\big).\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"Keadaan Bell logik yang digunakan dalam eksperimen ialah:\n"
"$$\n"
"|\\Phi^+\\rangle_L = \\tfrac{1}{\\sqrt 2}\\big(|00\\rangle_L + |11\\rangle_L\\big),\n"
"$$\n"
"analog bagi keadaan Bell piawai $\\tfrac{1}{\\sqrt 2}(|00\\rangle + |11\\rangle)$ pada dua qubit logik. Menggantikan ungkapan perkataan kod di atas memberikan bentuk empat qubit fizikalnya:\n"
"$$\n"
"|\\Phi^+\\rangle_L = \\tfrac{1}{2}\\big(|0000\\rangle + |1111\\rangle + |0110\\rangle + |1001\\rangle\\big).\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The preparation circuit applies two H + CNOT pairs, on $(q_0, q_3)$ and $(q_1, q_2)$. Each pair produces a physical Bell state $\\tfrac{1}{\\sqrt 2}(|00\\rangle + |11\\rangle)$ on its two qubits, so the full four-qubit output is the tensor product:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\tfrac{1}{2}\\big(|00\\rangle + |11\\rangle\\big)_{q_0 q_3} \\otimes \\big(|00\\rangle + |11\\rangle\\big)_{q_1 q_2}.\n"
"$$\n"
"Expanding this tensor product, the four computational-basis strings that appear with equal amplitude are $|0000\\rangle, |1111\\rangle, |0110\\rangle, |1001\\rangle$, the same four strings that appear in the expression for $|\\Phi^+\\rangle_L$ above. The circuit therefore prepares $|\\Phi^+\\rangle_L$ directly.\n"
msgstr ""
"Litar penyediaan menggunakan dua pasangan H + CNOT, pada $(q_0, q_3)$ dan $(q_1, q_2)$. Setiap pasangan menghasilkan keadaan Bell fizikal $\\tfrac{1}{\\sqrt 2}(|00\\rangle + |11\\rangle)$ pada dua qubitnya, maka output empat qubit penuh ialah hasil darab tensor:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\tfrac{1}{2}\\big(|00\\rangle + |11\\rangle\\big)_{q_0 q_3} \\otimes \\big(|00\\rangle + |11\\rangle\\big)_{q_1 q_2}.\n"
"$$\n"
"Mengembangkan hasil darab tensor ini, empat rentetan asas pengiraan yang muncul dengan amplitud sama ialah $|0000\\rangle, |1111\\rangle, |0110\\rangle, |1001\\rangle$, iaitu empat rentetan yang sama yang muncul dalam ungkapan bagi $|\\Phi^+\\rangle_L$ di atas. Litar ini oleh itu menyediakan $|\\Phi^+\\rangle_L$ secara langsung.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"</Accordion>\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We start by building the circuit that prepares the logical Bell state $|\\Phi^+\\rangle_L$. The construction uses two H + CNOT pairs to create two physical Bell pairs: one between data qubits 0 and 3, the other between data qubits 1 and 2. Their tensor product lies inside the $[[4,2,2]]$ codespace and is equal to $|\\Phi^+\\rangle_L$ as defined in the previous section.\n"
msgstr "Kita mulakan dengan membina litar yang menyediakan keadaan Bell logik $|\\Phi^+\\rangle_L$. Pembinaan ini menggunakan dua pasangan H + CNOT untuk mencipta dua pasangan Bell fizikal: satu antara qubit data 0 dan 3, satu lagi antara qubit data 1 dan 2. Hasil darab tensor keduanya terletak dalam ruang kod $[[4,2,2]]$ dan sama dengan $|\\Phi^+\\rangle_L$ seperti yang ditakrifkan dalam bahagian sebelumnya.\n"

