# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "1.2.1 Simulator validation {#121-simulator-validation}"
msgstr "1.2.1 Pengesahan simulator {#121-simulator-validation}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Before running on hardware, we verify the syndrome extraction on a noiseless simulator. We prepare the logical Bell state $|\\Phi^+\\rangle_L$ and measure both stabilizers, $Z_3 Z_2 Z_1 Z_0$ and $X_3 X_2 X_1 X_0$, onto separate ancillas. Since $|\\Phi^+\\rangle_L$ lies in the codespace, both syndrome bits should return `0` deterministically.\n"
msgstr "Sebelum menjalankan pada perkakasan, kita mengesahkan pengekstrakan sindrom pada simulator tanpa hingar. Kita menyediakan keadaan Bell logik $|\\Phi^+\\rangle_L$ dan mengukur kedua-dua penstabil, $Z_3 Z_2 Z_1 Z_0$ dan $X_3 X_2 X_1 X_0$, ke atas ancilla yang berasingan. Oleh kerana $|\\Phi^+\\rangle_L$ terletak dalam ruang kod, kedua-dua bit sindrom sepatutnya memulangkan `0` secara deterministik.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Both syndrome bits return `0` deterministically on the clean logical Bell state, confirming that $|\\Phi^+\\rangle_L$ lies in the simultaneous $+1$ eigenspace of $Z_3 Z_2 Z_1 Z_0$ and $X_3 X_2 X_1 X_0$, that is, in the codespace.\n"
msgstr "Kedua-dua bit sindrom memulangkan `0` secara deterministik pada keadaan Bell logik yang bersih, mengesahkan bahawa $|\\Phi^+\\rangle_L$ terletak dalam ruang eigen $+1$ serentak bagi $Z_3 Z_2 Z_1 Z_0$ dan $X_3 X_2 X_1 X_0$, iaitu dalam ruang kod.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Before moving to hardware, we walk through how the two stabilizers respond to single-qubit Pauli errors. A stabilizer measurement returns $-1$ (syndrome bit `1`) when the error operator anti-commutes with the stabilizer, and $+1$ (syndrome bit `0`) when it commutes. This follows from how Pauli operators act on eigenstates: if $S|\\psi\\rangle = +|\\psi\\rangle$ and $E$ anti-commutes with $S$ ($ES = -SE$), then $S(E|\\psi\\rangle) = -E S|\\psi\\rangle = -E|\\psi\\rangle$, so the corrupted state $E|\\psi\\rangle$ is a $-1$ eigenstate of $S$.\n"
msgstr "Sebelum beralih ke perkakasan, kita lihat bagaimana kedua-dua penstabil bertindak balas terhadap ralat Pauli qubit tunggal. Pengukuran penstabil memulangkan $-1$ (bit sindrom `1`) apabila pengendali ralat anti-kalis tukar tertib dengan penstabil, dan $+1$ (bit sindrom `0`) apabila ia kalis tukar tertib. Ini berpunca daripada cara pengendali Pauli bertindak pada keadaan eigen: jika $S|\\psi\\rangle = +|\\psi\\rangle$ dan $E$ anti-kalis tukar tertib dengan $S$ ($ES = -SE$), maka $S(E|\\psi\\rangle) = -E S|\\psi\\rangle = -E|\\psi\\rangle$, jadi keadaan rosak $E|\\psi\\rangle$ ialah keadaan eigen $-1$ bagi $S$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We verify this directly on the simulator by injecting $X$, $Z$, and $Y$ errors on different data qubits and reading both syndrome bits.\n"
msgstr "Kita mengesahkan ini secara langsung pada simulator dengan menyuntik ralat $X$, $Z$, dan $Y$ pada qubit data yang berbeza dan membaca kedua-dua bit sindrom.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The simulation confirms the anti-commutation analysis: every single-qubit $X$ error gives the same syndrome regardless of which data qubit it hits, and similarly for $Z$ and $Y$. The four possible outcomes of the two-bit syndrome correspond cleanly to four error classes (the table below lists the syndrome bits as $(s_X, s_Z)$, matching the displayed [bitstring order convention in Qiskit](/guides/bit-ordering) `c[1] c[0]`):\n"
msgstr "Simulasi mengesahkan analisis anti-kalis tukar tertib: setiap ralat $X$ qubit tunggal memberikan sindrom yang sama tanpa mengira qubit data mana yang terkena, dan begitu juga bagi $Z$ dan $Y$. Empat hasil mungkin bagi sindrom dua bit sepadan dengan jelas kepada empat kelas ralat (jadual di bawah menyenaraikan bit sindrom sebagai $(s_X, s_Z)$, sepadan dengan [konvensyen tertib rentetan bit dalam Qiskit](/guides/bit-ordering) yang dipaparkan `c[1] c[0]`):\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Error on any single data qubit | $s_X$ | $s_Z$ |\n"
"|:---:|:---:|:---:|\n"
"| no error | `0` | `0` |\n"
"| $X$ | `0` | `1` |\n"
"| $Z$ | `1` | `0` |\n"
"| $Y$ | `1` | `1` |\n"
msgstr ""
"| Ralat pada mana-mana satu qubit data | $s_X$ | $s_Z$ |\n"
"|:---:|:---:|:---:|\n"
"| tiada ralat | `0` | `0` |\n"
"| $X$ | `0` | `1` |\n"
"| $Z$ | `1` | `0` |\n"
"| $Y$ | `1` | `1` |\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Two limitations of this scheme are worth stating now. First, the table identifies the *type* of error ($X$, $Z$, $Y$, or none) but not the *qubit* on which the error occurred: an $X$ error on data qubit 0 and an $X$ error on data qubit 2 produce identical syndromes, as the simulation shows directly. Without knowing the qubit location we cannot apply a corresponding inverse to undo the error, which is why we use the $[[4,2,2]]$ code for detection only: we post-select on $s_X = s_Z = 0$ and do not attempt correction. Second, the table covers only single-qubit errors; certain weight-2 errors commute with both stabilizers and escape the syndrome entirely. We return to that limitation in [Section 1.3](#limitations).\n"
msgstr "Dua had skim ini wajar dinyatakan sekarang. Pertama, jadual mengenal pasti *jenis* ralat ($X$, $Z$, $Y$, atau tiada) tetapi bukan *qubit* tempat ralat berlaku: ralat $X$ pada qubit data 0 dan ralat $X$ pada qubit data 2 menghasilkan sindrom yang serupa, seperti yang ditunjukkan secara langsung oleh simulasi. Tanpa mengetahui lokasi qubit, kita tidak dapat menggunakan songsangan sepadan untuk membatalkan ralat, itulah sebabnya kita menggunakan kod $[[4,2,2]]$ untuk pengesanan sahaja: kita melakukan pasca-pemilihan pada $s_X = s_Z = 0$ dan tidak cuba membetulkan. Kedua, jadual hanya meliputi ralat qubit tunggal; ralat berpemberat-2 tertentu kalis tukar tertib dengan kedua-dua penstabil dan terlepas sepenuhnya daripada sindrom. Kita kembali kepada had itu dalam [Bahagian 1.3](#limitations).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Check your understanding {#check-your-understanding-1}"
msgstr "Semak kefahaman anda {#check-your-understanding-1}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We just saw that an $X$ error flips the $Z_3Z_2Z_1Z_0$ syndrome, and a $Z$ error would flip the $X_3X_2X_1X_0$ syndrome. What happens if a $Y$ error hits a single data qubit? Which stabilizer or stabilizers would detect it?\n"
msgstr "Kita baru sahaja melihat bahawa ralat $X$ membalikkan sindrom $Z_3Z_2Z_1Z_0$, dan ralat $Z$ akan membalikkan sindrom $X_3X_2X_1X_0$. Apakah yang berlaku jika ralat $Y$ mengenai satu qubit data? Penstabil yang mana satu atau kedua-duanya akan mengesannya?\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "*Hint:* $Y = iXZ$, so a $Y$ error is both a bit-flip and a phase-flip on the same qubit.\n"
msgstr "*Petunjuk:* $Y = iXZ$, jadi ralat $Y$ ialah pembalikan bit dan pembalikan fasa pada qubit yang sama.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Since $Y = iXZ$, it anti-commutes with both $Z$-type and $X$-type stabilizer operators on the affected qubit. A single $Y$ error therefore triggers both stabilizers at once, giving syndrome $s_Z = 1$ and $s_X = 1$. The four single-qubit Pauli outcomes (none, $X$, $Z$, $Y$) map to four distinct syndrome patterns, as the simulation above confirms.\n"
msgstr "Oleh kerana $Y = iXZ$, ia anti-kalis tukar tertib dengan pengendali penstabil jenis-$Z$ dan jenis-$X$ pada qubit yang terjejas. Satu ralat $Y$ oleh itu mencetuskan kedua-dua penstabil serentak, memberikan sindrom $s_Z = 1$ dan $s_X = 1$. Empat hasil Pauli qubit tunggal (tiada, $X$, $Z$, $Y$) dipetakan kepada empat corak sindrom yang berbeza, seperti yang disahkan oleh simulasi di atas.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "1.2.2 Hardware demonstration: joint $Z$ and $X$ syndrome extraction {#122-hardware-demonstration-joint-z-and-x-syndrome-extraction}"
msgstr "1.2.2 Demonstrasi perkakasan: pengekstrakan sindrom $Z$ dan $X$ bersama {#122-hardware-demonstration-joint-z-and-x-syndrome-extraction}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We now run the same circuit on hardware and quantify the trade-off introduced by post-selecting on $s_X = s_Z = 0$. The metrics we report are the post-selection rate $A$ (fraction of shots that pass both checks), the sampling overhead $1/A$, and the Hellinger fidelity to the ideal data-qubit distribution before and after post-selection.\n"
msgstr "Kita sekarang menjalankan litar yang sama pada perkakasan dan mengukur pertukaran yang diperkenalkan oleh pasca-pemilihan pada $s_X = s_Z = 0$. Metrik yang kita laporkan ialah kadar pasca-pemilihan $A$ (pecahan syot yang lulus kedua-dua semakan), overhed pensampelan $1/A$, dan kesetiaan Hellinger kepada taburan qubit data unggul sebelum dan selepas pasca-pemilihan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The hardware circuit reuses the syndrome-extraction circuit `qc_check` built in the simulator validation above and adds measurements on the four data qubits at the end, in keeping with the end-of-circuit detection scope in Part 1. The two registers are kept separate: the syndrome bits land in `c` ($s_Z = c[0]$, $s_X = c[1]$), and the four data bits land in a new register `data_c`.\n"
msgstr "Litar perkakasan menggunakan semula litar pengekstrakan sindrom `qc_check` yang dibina dalam pengesahan simulator di atas dan menambah pengukuran pada empat qubit data di hujung, selaras dengan skop pengesanan hujung-litar dalam Bahagian 1. Kedua-dua daftar dikekalkan berasingan: bit sindrom diletakkan dalam `c` ($s_Z = c[0]$, $s_X = c[1]$), dan empat bit data diletakkan dalam daftar baharu `data_c`.\n"

