#, no-wrap
msgid "Submit the circuit. Wait for completion before proceeding.\n"
msgstr "Serahkan litar. Tunggu sehingga selesai sebelum meneruskan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Parse the six-bit results into the two syndromes ($s_Z$, $s_X$) and the four data bits, then apply each post-selection filter independently.\n"
msgstr "Huraikan keputusan enam bit kepada dua sindrom ($s_Z$, $s_X$) dan empat bit data, kemudian gunakan setiap penapis pasca-pemilihan secara berasingan.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/tools-for-quantum-advantage/error-correction-i/extracted-outputs/a446654c-1.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/tools-for-quantum-advantage/error-correction-i/extracted-outputs/a446654c-1.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In the saved run, post-selection improves the measured Hellinger fidelity, with the highest value obtained when both syndromes pass. Requiring both checks also gives the lowest acceptance, so the improvement comes at the cost of fewer usable shots. This measures agreement of the final Z-basis distribution with the ideal distribution, rather than certifying the full quantum state. On another backend or calibration, compare the fidelity and acceptance again. Requiring both syndromes always keeps a subset of the shots accepted by either check alone, but the fidelity ordering can change.\n"
msgstr "Dalam larian yang disimpan, pasca-pemilihan meningkatkan kesetiaan Hellinger yang diukur, dengan nilai tertinggi diperoleh apabila kedua-dua sindrom lulus. Memerlukan kedua-dua semakan juga memberikan kadar penerimaan yang terendah, maka peningkatan itu datang dengan kos syot yang boleh digunakan lebih sedikit. Ini mengukur persetujuan taburan asas-Z akhir dengan taburan unggul, dan bukannya mengesahkan keseluruhan keadaan kuantum. Pada backend atau penentukuran lain, bandingkan semula kesetiaan dan kadar penerimaan. Memerlukan kedua-dua sindrom sentiasa mengekalkan subset syot yang diterima oleh sama ada semakan sahaja, tetapi tertib kesetiaan boleh berubah.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Check your understanding {#check-your-understanding-2}"
msgstr "Semak kefahaman anda {#check-your-understanding-2}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Suppose $X$ errors strike both qubit $0$ and qubit $1$ simultaneously ($X_0 X_1$). What syndrome would $Z_3Z_2Z_1Z_0$ produce? Would $X_3X_2X_1X_0$ catch it? Would the error be detected at all?\n"
msgstr "Andaikan ralat $X$ mengenai qubit $0$ dan qubit $1$ serentak ($X_0 X_1$). Apakah sindrom yang akan dihasilkan oleh $Z_3Z_2Z_1Z_0$? Adakah $X_3X_2X_1X_0$ akan menangkapnya? Adakah ralat itu akan dikesan langsung?\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For $Z_3Z_2Z_1Z_0$: each $X$ flips one qubit's contribution to the $Z$-eigenvalue, and two flips cancel, so $Z_3Z_2Z_1Z_0$ returns $+1$ (syndrome bit `0`). For $X_3X_2X_1X_0$: $X_0 X_1$ commutes with $X_3X_2X_1X_0$ (both are products of $X$s), so $X_3X_2X_1X_0$ also returns $+1$. The error goes undetected. This is the $d=2$ shortcoming: $X_0 X_1$ is a weight-$2$ logical operator that maps one valid codeword to another without leaving the codespace.\n"
msgstr "Bagi $Z_3Z_2Z_1Z_0$: setiap $X$ membalikkan sumbangan satu qubit kepada nilai eigen $Z$, dan dua pembalikan saling membatalkan, maka $Z_3Z_2Z_1Z_0$ memulangkan $+1$ (bit sindrom `0`). Bagi $X_3X_2X_1X_0$: $X_0 X_1$ kalis tukar tertib dengan $X_3X_2X_1X_0$ (kedua-duanya hasil darab $X$), maka $X_3X_2X_1X_0$ juga memulangkan $+1$. Ralat itu tidak dikesan. Inilah kelemahan $d=2$: $X_0 X_1$ ialah pengendali logik berpemberat-$2$ yang memetakan satu perkataan kod yang sah kepada yang lain tanpa meninggalkan ruang kod.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-27
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"</Accordion>\n"
"Consider two errors: $X_0$ (single bit-flip on qubit $0$) and $X_1$ (single bit-flip on qubit $1$). Both are weight-$1$ errors that the $[[4,2,2]]$ code does detect. Can the code also tell them apart, that is, can it identify *which* qubit was hit?\n"
msgstr ""
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"</Accordion>\n"
"Pertimbangkan dua ralat: $X_0$ (pembalikan bit tunggal pada qubit $0$) dan $X_1$ (pembalikan bit tunggal pada qubit $1$). Kedua-duanya ialah ralat berpemberat-$1$ yang dikesan oleh kod $[[4,2,2]]$. Bolehkah kod itu juga membezakan keduanya, iaitu, bolehkah ia mengenal pasti qubit *yang mana* terkena?\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "No. Both $X_0$ and $X_1$ produce the same syndrome, $s_Z = 1$ and $s_X = 0$. The two-bit syndrome identifies that an $X$-type error happened, but not *which* qubit was affected. Equivalently, $X_0$ and $X_1$ differ by the logical operator $\\bar X_1 = X_0 X_1$, and logical operators are invisible to stabilizer measurements, so $X_0$ and $X_1 = X_0 \\cdot (X_0 X_1)$ look identical to the syndrome.\n"
msgstr "Tidak. Kedua-dua $X_0$ dan $X_1$ menghasilkan sindrom yang sama, $s_Z = 1$ dan $s_X = 0$. Sindrom dua bit mengenal pasti bahawa ralat jenis-$X$ telah berlaku, tetapi bukan qubit *yang mana* terjejas. Setara dengan itu, $X_0$ dan $X_1$ berbeza melalui pengendali logik $\\bar X_1 = X_0 X_1$, dan pengendali logik tidak kelihatan kepada pengukuran penstabil, jadi $X_0$ dan $X_1 = X_0 \\cdot (X_0 X_1)$ kelihatan serupa kepada sindrom.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This is why we use the $[[4,2,2]]$ code for detection only: it cannot correct an arbitrary single-qubit error. Codes with $d \\geq 3$, such as the Steane $[[7,1,3]]$ code, can correct any single-qubit error with ideal syndrome extraction.\n"
msgstr "Inilah sebabnya kita menggunakan kod $[[4,2,2]]$ untuk pengesanan sahaja: ia tidak dapat membetulkan ralat qubit tunggal yang sewenang-wenang. Kod dengan $d \\geq 3$, seperti kod Steane $[[7,1,3]]$, boleh membetulkan sebarang ralat qubit tunggal dengan pengekstrakan sindrom unggul.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"</Accordion>\n"
"The post-selection filter keeps shots where both syndrome bits read $0$, but passing the filter is not the same as correctness: some accepted shots can still land outside the ideal support of $|\\Phi^+\\rangle_L$. The cell below extracts these *false-accept* shots from the hardware data and breaks them into two categories: those whose data bitstrings have even parity but lie outside the target support, and those with odd parity. These are categories of computational-basis outcomes, not a test of whether the quantum state was in the codespace.\n"
msgstr ""
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"</Accordion>\n"
"Penapis pasca-pemilihan mengekalkan syot yang kedua-dua bit sindromnya bernilai $0$, tetapi lulus penapis tidak sama dengan betul: sesetengah syot yang diterima masih boleh jatuh di luar sokongan unggul $|\\Phi^+\\rangle_L$. Sel di bawah mengekstrak syot *terima-palsu* ini daripada data perkakasan dan membahagikannya kepada dua kategori: yang rentetan bit datanya berpariti genap tetapi terletak di luar sokongan sasaran, dan yang berpariti ganjil. Ini ialah kategori hasil asas pengiraan, bukan ujian sama ada keadaan kuantum berada dalam ruang kod.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The false-accept shots could have arisen from several mechanisms: readout errors on the data or ancilla qubits, gate errors in the syndrome circuit, weight-$2$ errors that the syndrome cannot detect, or non-Pauli errors such as energy relaxation, which a stabilizer measurement catches only with some probability. The \"closest ideal(s)\" column compares bitstrings, but it does not identify which of these mechanisms occurred or certify that the quantum state was in the codespace. [Section 1.3](#limitations) takes up these limits.\n"
msgstr "Syot terima-palsu boleh timbul daripada beberapa mekanisme: ralat bacaan pada qubit data atau ancilla, ralat get dalam litar sindrom, ralat berpemberat-$2$ yang tidak dapat dikesan oleh sindrom, atau ralat bukan Pauli seperti relaksasi tenaga, yang hanya ditangkap oleh pengukuran penstabil dengan kebarangkalian tertentu. Lajur \"ideal terdekat\" membandingkan rentetan bit, tetapi ia tidak mengenal pasti mekanisme mana yang berlaku atau mengesahkan bahawa keadaan kuantum berada dalam ruang kod. [Bahagian 1.3](#limitations) membincangkan had ini.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Readout error mitigation techniques such as M3 or TREX could be applied to reduce the readout contribution and obtain higher-fidelity post-selected results.\n"
msgstr "Teknik mitigasi ralat bacaan seperti M3 atau TREX boleh digunakan untuk mengurangkan sumbangan bacaan dan memperoleh keputusan berpasca-pemilihan berkesetiaan lebih tinggi.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Check your understanding {#check-your-understanding-3}"
msgstr "Semak kefahaman anda {#check-your-understanding-3}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A stabilizer code has parameters $[[n, k, d]]$ with $r = n - k$ stabilizer generators. Suppose we want to encode more logical qubits at the same distance. Must the number of stabilizer generators increase, and what determines the syndrome-extraction cost?\n"
msgstr "Kod penstabil mempunyai parameter $[[n, k, d]]$ dengan $r = n - k$ penjana penstabil. Andaikan kita mahu mengekod lebih banyak qubit logik pada jarak yang sama. Adakah bilangan penjana penstabil mesti meningkat, dan apakah yang menentukan kos pengekstrakan sindrom?\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Not necessarily: $r = n - k$ need not increase with $k$. For example, even-$n$ codes with $n \\geq 4$ and generators $X^{\\otimes n}$ and $Z^{\\otimes n}$ have parameters $[[n,n-2,2]]$: they keep two generators while their weights grow. Syndrome-extraction cost depends on the number and weights of the generators, routing, and whether ancillas are reused. Two-qubit gates are typically a major noise source on near-term hardware, so a larger extraction circuit can introduce more noise and reduce the post-selection rate.\n"
msgstr "Belum tentu: $r = n - k$ tidak semestinya meningkat dengan $k$. Contohnya, kod dengan $n$ genap dan $n \\geq 4$ serta penjana $X^{\\otimes n}$ dan $Z^{\\otimes n}$ mempunyai parameter $[[n,n-2,2]]$: kod ini mengekalkan dua penjana walaupun pemberatnya bertambah. Kos pengekstrakan sindrom bergantung pada bilangan dan pemberat penjana, penghalaan, dan sama ada ancilla digunakan semula. Gate dua-qubit lazimnya merupakan punca hingar utama pada perkakasan jangka dekat, jadi litar pengekstrakan yang lebih besar boleh menambah hingar dan merendahkan kadar pasca-pemilihan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The following examples illustrate different encoding rates and generator counts:\n"
msgstr "Contoh berikut menggambarkan kadar pengekodan dan bilangan penjana yang berbeza:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Code | $n$ | $k$ | $d$ | Encoding rate $k/n$ | Stabilizer generators |\n"
"|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n"
"| $[[4,2,2]]$ | 4 | 2 | 2 | 0.50 | 2 |\n"
"| $[[5,1,3]]$ | 5 | 1 | 3 | 0.20 | 4 |\n"
"| $[[7,1,3]]$ (Steane) | 7 | 1 | 3 | 0.14 | 6 |\n"
"| $[[9,1,3]]$ (Shor) | 9 | 1 | 3 | 0.11 | 8 |\n"
msgstr ""
"| Kod | $n$ | $k$ | $d$ | Kadar pengekodan $k/n$ | Penjana penstabil |\n"
"|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n"
"| $[[4,2,2]]$ | 4 | 2 | 2 | 0.50 | 2 |\n"
"| $[[5,1,3]]$ | 5 | 1 | 3 | 0.20 | 4 |\n"
"| $[[7,1,3]]$ (Steane) | 7 | 1 | 3 | 0.14 | 6 |\n"
"| $[[9,1,3]]$ (Shor) | 9 | 1 | 3 | 0.11 | 8 |\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In these examples, the distance-$3$ codes use more stabilizer generators and have lower encoding rates than the $[[4,2,2]]$ code. This comparison is not a universal scaling rule. The cost of code-based detection depends on the chosen code and its implementation.\n"
msgstr "Dalam contoh ini, kod jarak-$3$ menggunakan lebih banyak penjana penstabil dan mempunyai kadar pengekodan yang lebih rendah daripada kod $[[4,2,2]]$. Perbandingan ini bukan petua penskalaan sejagat. Kos pengesanan berasaskan kod bergantung pada kod yang dipilih dan pelaksanaannya.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"</AccordionItem>\n"
