msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "1.3 Limits of end-of-circuit detection {#13-limits-of-end-of-circuit-detection}"
msgstr "1.3 Had pengesanan di hujung litar {#13-limits-of-end-of-circuit-detection}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "So far we have looked at end-of-circuit post-selection through two examples: bitstring filtering ([Section 1.1](#symmetry-post-selection)) and stabilizer-code post-selection ([Section 1.2](#stabilizer-code)). Three limitations follow from the architecture they share.\n"
msgstr "Setakat ini kita telah melihat pasca-pemilihan di hujung litar melalui dua contoh: penapisan rentetan bit ([Bahagian 1.1](#symmetry-post-selection)) dan pasca-pemilihan kod penstabil ([Bahagian 1.2](#stabilizer-code)). Tiga had timbul daripada seni bina yang mereka kongsi.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Some errors are not flagged**\n"
msgstr "**Sesetengah ralat tidak ditandakan**\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "With $d = 2$, weight-$2$ Pauli operators that act non-trivially on the encoded data can commute with both stabilizers and therefore go undetected. The reach is set by the code distance: detecting more errors of higher weight requires a code with larger $d$.\n"
msgstr "Dengan $d = 2$, operator Pauli berpemberat-$2$ yang bertindak secara tak remeh pada data terkod boleh berkalis tukar tertib dengan kedua-dua penstabil dan oleh itu tidak dikesan. Jangkauannya ditentukan oleh jarak kod: mengesan lebih banyak ralat berpemberat lebih tinggi memerlukan kod dengan $d$ yang lebih besar.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**The syndrome does not localize the fault**\n"
msgstr "**Sindrom tidak menentukan lokasi kerosakan**\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "When a syndrome bit fires, the syndrome record tells us that something went wrong somewhere in the circuit but not on which qubit, in which gate layer, or whether the underlying fault was a gate error in the payload, a gate error in the syndrome extraction, or a measurement readout error on the data or ancilla qubits. The single-shot ambiguity reported in the false-accept table (multiple ideal codewords often equally close in bitstring distance) is consistent with the same limit.\n"
msgstr "Apabila bit sindrom menyala, rekod sindrom memberitahu kita bahawa ada sesuatu yang tidak kena di suatu tempat dalam litar, tetapi tidak pada qubit yang mana, dalam lapisan gate yang mana, atau sama ada kerosakan asasnya ialah ralat gate dalam muatan, ralat gate dalam pengekstrakan sindrom, atau ralat bacaan pengukuran pada qubit data atau ancilla. Kekaburan satu-tembakan yang dilaporkan dalam jadual penerimaan palsu (beberapa kata kod ideal sering sama dekat dari segi jarak rentetan bit) selaras dengan had yang sama.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Detection itself adds gates**\n"
msgstr "**Pengesanan itu sendiri menambah gate**\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "At the logical level, the $|\\Phi^+\\rangle_L$ preparation uses four gates (two H + two CNOT), and the joint $Z_3 Z_2 Z_1 Z_0$ + $X_3 X_2 X_1 X_0$ syndrome extraction adds 16 logical gates (four CNOT for Z-check + 12 gates for X-check with Hadamard conjugation) and two ancilla qubits. However, transpilation to hardware-native gates increases these counts, as the cell below demonstrates.\n"
msgstr "Pada peringkat logik, penyediaan $|\\Phi^+\\rangle_L$ menggunakan empat gate (dua H + dua CNOT), dan pengekstrakan sindrom bersama $Z_3 Z_2 Z_1 Z_0$ + $X_3 X_2 X_1 X_0$ menambah 16 gate logik (empat CNOT untuk semakan Z + 12 gate untuk semakan X dengan konjugasi Hadamard) dan dua qubit ancilla. Namun, transpilasi kepada gate asli perkakasan meningkatkan kiraan ini, seperti yang ditunjukkan oleh sel di bawah.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This example is intentionally extreme. In the $[[4,2,2]]$ code, the $|\\Phi^+\\rangle_L$ preparation here uses only four logical gates, so the syndrome-extraction block makes up most of the transpiled circuit. The gate-count comparison above illustrates a large relative overhead. When the payload is minimal, syndrome extraction can dominate the total gate count. In a payload with many more gates, the same fixed-size syndrome block would be a smaller fraction of the total. The conclusion that the syndrome-extraction circuit is itself noisy still holds, even though the ratio above does not.\n"
msgstr "Contoh ini sengaja dibuat ekstrem. Dalam kod $[[4,2,2]]$, penyediaan $|\\Phi^+\\rangle_L$ di sini hanya menggunakan empat gate logik, jadi blok pengekstrakan sindrom membentuk sebahagian besar litar yang ditranspil. Perbandingan kiraan gate di atas menggambarkan overhed relatif yang besar. Apabila muatan adalah minimum, pengekstrakan sindrom boleh mendominasi jumlah kiraan gate. Dalam muatan dengan lebih banyak gate, blok sindrom bersaiz tetap yang sama akan menjadi pecahan yang lebih kecil daripada jumlah. Kesimpulan bahawa litar pengekstrakan sindrom itu sendiri bersifat bising tetap benar, walaupun nisbah di atas tidak.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The cost depends on the code's stabilizer count and weights, routing, and ancilla reuse (note the scaling question above). As target circuits grow toward utility scale (40+ qubits), end-of-circuit code-based detection in this direct form might not be the most efficient option on near-term hardware.\n"
msgstr "Kos bergantung pada bilangan dan pemberat penstabil kod, penghalaan, dan penggunaan semula ancilla (perhatikan soalan penskalaan di atas). Apabila litar sasaran berkembang ke skala utiliti (40+ qubit), pengesanan berasaskan kod di hujung litar dalam bentuk langsung ini mungkin bukan pilihan paling cekap pada perkakasan jangka dekat.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Part 2: Mid-circuit detection {#part-2-mid-circuit-detection}"
msgstr "Bahagian 2: Pengesanan pertengahan litar {#part-2-mid-circuit-detection}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "[Section 1.3](#limitations) listed three limitations of end-of-circuit detection: certain weight-2 errors go undetected, the syndrome does not localize the fault, and a fixed syndrome-extraction block is applied to every shot. In Part 2, we move detection inside the circuit and partially address the third limitation. Checks couple ancillas to the data at selected circuit locations, including interior points. In these examples, the ancillas are measured at the end alongside the data, and post-selection happens in classical post-processing. When lighter checks are distributed across multiple interior points, the per-shot gate cost can track the circuit structure rather than a fixed code block. Some faults still pass undetected, and these checks do not in general identify a unique fault location.\n"
msgstr "[Bahagian 1.3](#limitations) menyenaraikan tiga had pengesanan di hujung litar: ralat berpemberat-2 tertentu tidak dikesan, sindrom tidak menentukan lokasi kerosakan, dan blok pengekstrakan sindrom tetap dikenakan pada setiap tembakan. Dalam Bahagian 2, kita memindahkan pengesanan ke dalam litar dan menangani had ketiga secara separa. Semakan mengganding ancilla dengan data pada lokasi litar terpilih, termasuk titik dalaman. Dalam contoh ini, ancilla diukur di hujung bersama data, dan pasca-pemilihan berlaku dalam pasca-pemprosesan klasik. Apabila semakan yang lebih ringan diedarkan merentasi beberapa titik dalaman, kos gate setiap tembakan boleh mengikut struktur litar dan bukannya blok kod tetap. Sesetengah kerosakan masih lepas tanpa dikesan, dan semakan ini secara umum tidak mengenal pasti lokasi kerosakan yang unik.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We work through two ideas:\n"
msgstr "Kita meneliti dua idea:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Coherent Pauli checks (Sections [2.2](#coherent)-[2.3](#spacetime)): the algebraic foundation. For any Clifford payload $U$ and post-payload check $R$, the pre-payload check $L = U^\\dagger R\\, U$ defines a valid check pair.\n"
msgstr "Semakan Pauli koheren (Bahagian [2.2](#coherent)-[2.3](#spacetime)): asas algebra. Bagi sebarang muatan Clifford $U$ dan semakan pasca-muatan $R$, semakan pra-muatan $L = U^\\dagger R\\, U$ mentakrifkan pasangan semakan yang sah.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Spacetime codes (Sections [2.4](#paulice)-[2.5](#hardware-experiment)): a hardware-aware refinement. Place lightweight checks at points in the circuit where the local stabilizer structure makes $L$ unnecessary, and trace their detection regions through the circuit graph.\n"
msgstr "Kod ruang-masa (Bahagian [2.4](#paulice)-[2.5](#hardware-experiment)): penambahbaikan yang peka perkakasan. Letakkan semakan ringan pada titik dalam litar yang struktur penstabil setempatnya menjadikan $L$ tidak diperlukan, dan jejaki kawasan pengesanannya melalui graf litar.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Both CPC and spacetime codes are designed for *Clifford circuits* (or circuits dominated by Clifford gates). The space of valid checks shrinks exponentially as non-Clifford content increases ([Martiel & Javadi-Abhari, 2025, Supp. V](https://arxiv.org/abs/2504.15725)). The random Clifford payload used in Part 2 is entirely Clifford, which is why it is a convenient testbed.\n"
msgstr "Kedua-dua CPC dan kod ruang-masa direka untuk *litar Clifford* (atau litar yang didominasi gate Clifford). Ruang semakan yang sah mengecil secara eksponen apabila kandungan bukan Clifford meningkat ([Martiel & Javadi-Abhari, 2025, Supp. V](https://arxiv.org/abs/2504.15725)). Muatan Clifford rawak yang digunakan dalam Bahagian 2 sepenuhnya Clifford, itulah sebabnya ia merupakan medan ujian yang sesuai.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "2.1 From end-of-circuit filtering to mid-circuit checks {#21-from-end-of-circuit-filtering-to-mid-circuit-checks}"
msgstr "2.1 Daripada penapisan di hujung litar kepada semakan pertengahan litar {#21-from-end-of-circuit-filtering-to-mid-circuit-checks}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "End-of-circuit post-selection collects all check information from a final measurement. The checks can only see the cumulative effect of errors across the entire circuit. Mid-circuit checks change *what* the detection can see. A check ancilla couples to the data at selected points during the circuit. In these examples it is measured at the end alongside the data, and post-selection rejects flagged shots in classical post-processing.\n"
msgstr "Pasca-pemilihan di hujung litar mengumpul semua maklumat semakan daripada pengukuran akhir. Semakan hanya dapat melihat kesan terkumpul ralat merentasi seluruh litar. Semakan pertengahan litar mengubah *apa* yang boleh dilihat oleh pengesanan. Ancilla semakan bergandingan dengan data pada titik terpilih semasa litar. Dalam contoh ini ia diukur di hujung bersama data, dan pasca-pemilihan menolak tembakan yang ditandakan dalam pasca-pemprosesan klasik.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The framework for mid-circuit checks is *coherent Pauli checks (CPC)*, introduced in [Section 2.2](#coherent). CPC tells us *what* to check and *why* the check is guaranteed to pass on an error-free circuit. The challenge is making these checks practical. A CPC-derived check can involve a high-weight Pauli operator spanning many qubits, which on a connectivity-constrained device requires routing gates that add more noise than the check removes. [Martiel & Javadi-Abhari (2025)](https://arxiv.org/abs/2504.15725) address this directly. *Spacetime codes* keep the same CPC algebra but constrain checks to be spatially local, spreading their sensitivity across many circuit layers instead of many qubits. This transition begins in Section 2.3.3 and is developed in Sections [2.4](#paulice)-[2.5](#hardware-experiment).\n"
msgstr "Rangka kerja untuk semakan pertengahan litar ialah *semakan Pauli koheren (CPC)*, yang diperkenalkan dalam [Bahagian 2.2](#coherent). CPC memberitahu kita *apa* yang perlu disemak dan *mengapa* semakan itu dijamin lulus pada litar tanpa ralat. Cabarannya ialah menjadikan semakan ini praktikal. Semakan terbitan CPC boleh melibatkan operator Pauli berpemberat tinggi yang merangkumi banyak qubit, yang pada peranti dengan kesambungan terhad memerlukan gate penghalaan yang menambah lebih banyak hingar daripada yang disingkirkan oleh semakan. [Martiel & Javadi-Abhari (2025)](https://arxiv.org/abs/2504.15725) menangani perkara ini secara langsung. *Kod ruang-masa* mengekalkan algebra CPC yang sama tetapi mengehadkan semakan kepada setempat secara ruang, menyebarkan kepekaannya merentasi banyak lapisan litar dan bukannya banyak qubit. Peralihan ini bermula dalam Bahagian 2.3.3 dan dibangunkan dalam Bahagian [2.4](#paulice)-[2.5](#hardware-experiment).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"What &quot;mid-circuit&quot; really means in this lesson\">\n"
msgstr ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Maksud sebenar &quot;pertengahan litar&quot; dalam pelajaran ini\">\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The benefit of a mid-circuit check is not the timing of the measurement, but the fact that *the check couples to the circuit at an interior point*, which means that its detection region can be tailored to selected parts of the payload. When we say \"mid-circuit check,\" think \"interior-coupled check with a spacetime detection region.\"\n"
msgstr "Manfaat semakan pertengahan litar bukanlah masa pengukuran, tetapi hakikat bahawa *semakan itu bergandingan dengan litar pada titik dalaman*, yang bermakna kawasan pengesanannya boleh disesuaikan untuk bahagian muatan yang dipilih. Apabila kita menyebut \"semakan pertengahan litar\", fikirkan \"semakan bergandingan dalaman dengan kawasan pengesanan ruang-masa\".\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In the [Section 2.5](#hardware-experiment) hardware experiment, each check ancilla couples to the payload at a few points along a target wire and is measured at the *end of the circuit* alongside the data qubits, not at an intermediate point with reset and reuse. Its sensitivity nevertheless extends *into the circuit interior* because the check operator propagates through the payload under conjugation (discussed in [Section 2.4](#paulice)). What we demonstrate is the spacetime-code principle, checks whose detection regions extend deep into the circuit's interior, even though the measurement happens at the boundary. A fully mid-circuit implementation (measure, reset, reuse) would further reduce idle time on ancillas and is an important engineering step. See [Lanes et al. (2025)](https://arxiv.org/abs/2506.20658) for how dynamic circuit capabilities enable these protocols at scale.\n"
msgstr "Dalam eksperimen perkakasan [Bahagian 2.5](#hardware-experiment), setiap ancilla semakan bergandingan dengan muatan pada beberapa titik di sepanjang wayar sasaran dan diukur pada *hujung litar* bersama qubit data, bukan pada titik perantaraan dengan set semula dan guna semula. Namun kepekaannya meluas *ke dalam bahagian dalam litar* kerana operator semakan merambat melalui muatan di bawah konjugasi (dibincangkan dalam [Bahagian 2.4](#paulice)). Apa yang kita tunjukkan ialah prinsip kod ruang-masa, iaitu semakan yang kawasan pengesanannya meluas jauh ke dalam bahagian dalam litar, walaupun pengukuran berlaku di sempadan. Pelaksanaan pertengahan litar sepenuhnya (ukur, set semula, guna semula) akan mengurangkan lagi masa melahu pada ancilla dan merupakan langkah kejuruteraan yang penting. Lihat [Lanes et al. (2025)](https://arxiv.org/abs/2506.20658) tentang bagaimana keupayaan litar dinamik membolehkan protokol ini pada skala besar.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Check your understanding {#check-your-understanding-4}"
msgstr "Semak kefahaman anda {#check-your-understanding-4}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A 40-qubit circuit has post-selection rate $A = 0.6$ with one mid-circuit check. How many raw shots do you need to collect 3,000 accepted shots? What happens to this number if you add a second independent check with the same per-check post-selection rate?\n"
msgstr "Litar 40-qubit mempunyai kadar pasca-pemilihan $A = 0.6$ dengan satu semakan pertengahan litar. Berapakah tembakan mentah yang anda perlu kumpulkan untuk mendapatkan 3,000 tembakan yang diterima? Apakah yang berlaku kepada nombor ini jika anda menambah semakan bebas kedua dengan kadar pasca-pemilihan setiap semakan yang sama?\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "With one check at $A = 0.6$, the sampling overhead is $1/A \\approx 1.67$, so you need $3\\,000 / 0.6 = 5\\,000$ raw shots.\n"
msgstr "Dengan satu semakan pada $A = 0.6$, overhed pensampelan ialah $1/A \\approx 1.67$, jadi anda memerlukan $3\\,000 / 0.6 = 5\\,000$ tembakan mentah.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "If a second independent check also passes 60% of shots, the combined post-selection rate is $A_\\text{combined} = 0.6 \\times 0.6 = 0.36$. Now you need $3\\,000 / 0.36 \\approx 8\\,334$ raw shots, about $1.67\\times$ the single-check case.\n"
msgstr "Jika semakan bebas kedua juga meluluskan 60% tembakan, kadar pasca-pemilihan gabungan ialah $A_\\text{combined} = 0.6 \\times 0.6 = 0.36$. Kini anda memerlukan $3\\,000 / 0.36 \\approx 8\\,334$ tembakan mentah, kira-kira $1.67\\times$ berbanding kes semakan tunggal.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This illustrates that each additional check multiplies the sampling cost, which shows that adding checks is not free. The fidelity gain from each extra check needs to justify the additional loss in post-selection rate. [Section 2.5](#hardware-experiment) examines this trade-off in real hardware data.\n"
msgstr "Ini menggambarkan bahawa setiap semakan tambahan mendarabkan kos pensampelan, yang menunjukkan bahawa menambah semakan tidak percuma. Peningkatan kesetiaan daripada setiap semakan tambahan perlu mewajarkan kehilangan tambahan dalam kadar pasca-pemilihan. [Bahagian 2.5](#hardware-experiment) meneliti pertukaran ini dalam data perkakasan sebenar.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "(Note: this calculation assumes check outcomes are independent. In practice, checks may share sensitivity to the same noise sources, so the combined post-selection rate can differ from the simple product.)\n"
msgstr "(Nota: pengiraan ini mengandaikan keputusan semakan adalah bebas. Dalam praktiknya, semakan mungkin berkongsi kepekaan terhadap punca hingar yang sama, jadi kadar pasca-pemilihan gabungan boleh berbeza daripada hasil darab ringkas.)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"</Accordion>\n"
"<span id=\"coherent\"></span>\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "2.2 Coherent Pauli checks (CPC) {#22-coherent-pauli-checks-cpc}"
msgstr "2.2 Semakan Pauli koheren (CPC) {#22-coherent-pauli-checks-cpc}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Coherent Pauli checks (CPC) provide a framework for what to check and why the check works.\n"
msgstr "Semakan Pauli koheren (CPC) menyediakan rangka kerja tentang apa yang perlu disemak dan mengapa semakan itu berfungsi.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Here we have a Clifford circuit $U$ (the *payload*) that we want to protect. We pick a Pauli operator $R$ and apply it to the payload's output through a controlled-Pauli gate from an ancilla. The pre-payload partner $L$, obtained by pulling $R$ back through $U$, is applied to the input through a second controlled-Pauli. In the ideal (error-free) circuit the two controlled-Paulis cancel coherently on the ancilla, so the ancilla measurement is deterministic. Errors between the two controlled-Paulis that anti-commute with the effective check operator break this cancellation and can flip the ancilla outcome.\n"
msgstr "Di sini kita mempunyai litar Clifford $U$ (*muatan*) yang ingin kita lindungi. Kita memilih operator Pauli $R$ dan mengenakannya pada keluaran muatan melalui gate Pauli terkawal daripada ancilla. Pasangan pra-muatan $L$, yang diperoleh dengan menarik $R$ ke belakang melalui $U$, dikenakan pada masukan melalui Pauli terkawal kedua. Dalam litar ideal (tanpa ralat), kedua-dua Pauli terkawal itu saling membatalkan secara koheren pada ancilla, jadi pengukuran ancilla bersifat deterministik. Ralat di antara kedua-dua Pauli terkawal yang berantikalis tukar tertib dengan operator semakan berkesan memecahkan pembatalan ini dan boleh membalikkan keputusan ancilla.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<Admonition type=\"note\" title=\"Two ways the deterministic outcome can arise\">\n"
msgstr "<Admonition type=\"note\" title=\"Dua cara keputusan deterministik boleh timbul\">\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "*State-preparation setting.* When $U$ is run on the standard input $|0\\rangle^{\\otimes n}$ and $R$ is chosen to be a stabilizer of the target output state $U|0\\rangle^{\\otimes n}$, then $R$ alone returns $+1$ on the ideal output. This is the case for the right-only checks in Section 2.3.3. An input stabilizer $Z_j$ pushed forward through the payload stabilizes the output state, so it returns $+1$ with no $L$ needed.\n"
msgstr "*Tetapan penyediaan keadaan.* Apabila $U$ dijalankan pada masukan piawai $|0\\rangle^{\\otimes n}$ dan $R$ dipilih sebagai penstabil keadaan keluaran sasaran $U|0\\rangle^{\\otimes n}$, maka $R$ sahaja memulangkan $+1$ pada keluaran ideal. Ini ialah kes bagi semakan kanan-sahaja dalam Bahagian 2.3.3. Penstabil masukan $Z_j$ yang ditolak ke hadapan melalui muatan menstabilkan keadaan keluaran, jadi ia memulangkan $+1$ tanpa memerlukan $L$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "*General CPC setting.* $R$ need *not* be a stabilizer by itself. The guarantee comes from the pair $(L, R)$: the coherent $L$-$U$-$R$ sandwich returns the ancilla to its starting value on an error-free circuit. If $R$ is not a stabilizer of the output, measuring it alone need not give a deterministic result. The *consistency* between $L$ and $R$ is checked, not the eigenvalue of either operator individually.\n"
msgstr "*Tetapan CPC am.* $R$ *tidak* semestinya penstabil dengan sendirinya. Jaminan datang daripada pasangan $(L, R)$: sandwic koheren $L$-$U$-$R$ memulangkan ancilla kepada nilai permulaannya pada litar tanpa ralat. Jika $R$ bukan penstabil bagi keluaran, mengukurnya sahaja belum tentu memberikan keputusan deterministik. *Ketekalan* antara $L$ dan $R$ yang disemak, bukan nilai eigen mana-mana operator secara individu.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In both settings the detection mechanism is the same.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"Dalam kedua-dua tetapan, mekanisme pengesanan adalah sama.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The detection mechanism is anti-commutation: an error anti-commuting with the check flips its outcome from $+1$ to $-1$, while an error commuting with the check passes undetected. (Concretely, $R = Z_0 Z_1$ catches $X$ or $Y$ on qubits 0-1 because $XZ = -ZX$, but misses $Z$-type errors there because $Z$ commutes with itself.)\n"
msgstr "Mekanisme pengesanan ialah antikalis tukar tertib: ralat yang berantikalis tukar tertib dengan semakan membalikkan keputusannya daripada $+1$ kepada $-1$, manakala ralat yang berkalis tukar tertib dengan semakan lulus tanpa dikesan. (Secara konkrit, $R = Z_0 Z_1$ menangkap $X$ atau $Y$ pada qubit 0-1 kerana $XZ = -ZX$, tetapi terlepas ralat jenis $Z$ di situ kerana $Z$ berkalis tukar tertib dengan dirinya sendiri.)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To see what this looks like in practice, and why it creates a scalability challenge, we build an example step by step.\n"
msgstr "Untuk melihat rupanya dalam praktik, dan mengapa ia mewujudkan cabaran kebolehskalaan, kita membina satu contoh langkah demi langkah.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
