# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "2.3.1 Anti-commutation rule {#231-anti-commutation-rule}"
msgstr "2.3.1 Peraturan antikalis tukar tertib {#231-anti-commutation-rule}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A CPC check detects an error if and only if the error *anti-commutes* with the check operator. For an error injected between $U_A$ and $U_B$, there are two equivalent ways to see it:\n"
msgstr "Semakan CPC mengesan ralat jika dan hanya jika ralat itu *berantikalis tukar tertib* dengan operator semakan. Bagi ralat yang disuntik di antara $U_A$ dan $U_B$, terdapat dua cara setara untuk melihatnya:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "*From $R$'s side:* the error propagates forward through $U_B$, arriving at $R$ as $U_B E U_B^\\dagger$. Detection depends on whether this commutes with $R$.\n"
msgstr "*Dari sisi $R$:* ralat merambat ke hadapan melalui $U_B$, tiba pada $R$ sebagai $U_B E U_B^\\dagger$. Pengesanan bergantung pada sama ada ini berkalis tukar tertib dengan $R$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "*From $L$'s side:* the error propagates backward through $U_A^\\dagger$, arriving at $L$ as $U_A^\\dagger E U_A$. Detection depends on whether this commutes with $L$.\n"
msgstr "*Dari sisi $L$:* ralat merambat ke belakang melalui $U_A^\\dagger$, tiba pada $L$ sebagai $U_A^\\dagger E U_A$. Pengesanan bergantung pada sama ada ini berkalis tukar tertib dengan $L$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Since $L = U^\\dagger R U$, these two conditions are algebraically equivalent: $L$ and $R$ always agree. We verify this:\n"
msgstr "Oleh kerana $L = U^\\dagger R U$, kedua-dua syarat ini setara secara algebra: $L$ dan $R$ sentiasa sepakat. Kita mengesahkannya:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "$L$ and $R$ always agree on each error: what one detects, the other detects too. Whether a given error is caught is not simply a matter of distance from the check's support: the rule is anti-commutation between the check operator and the error at the location it is evaluated. Some errors near the support are caught, others commute with the check there and pass. Errors far from the support often propagate through too few gates to reach $R$ as a non-trivial operator, and so they pass as well.\n"
msgstr "$L$ dan $R$ sentiasa sepakat pada setiap ralat: apa yang dikesan oleh satu, dikesan juga oleh yang lain. Sama ada sesuatu ralat ditangkap bukan sekadar soal jarak dari sokongan semakan: peraturannya ialah antikalis tukar tertib antara operator semakan dan ralat pada lokasi penilaiannya. Sesetengah ralat berhampiran sokongan ditangkap, yang lain berkalis tukar tertib dengan semakan di situ dan lulus. Ralat yang jauh dari sokongan sering merambat melalui terlalu sedikit gate untuk sampai pada $R$ sebagai operator tak remeh, lalu ia juga lulus.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Now we quantify this: each of the 20 qubits can suffer an $X$, $Y$, or $Z$ error, giving $20 \\times 3 = 60$ possible single-qubit errors at the mid-circuit location. How many does this single CPC pair catch?\n"
msgstr "Sekarang kita mengukurnya: setiap satu daripada 20 qubit boleh mengalami ralat $X$, $Y$, atau $Z$, memberikan $20 \\times 3 = 60$ kemungkinan ralat qubit tunggal pada lokasi pertengahan litar. Berapa banyak yang ditangkap oleh satu pasangan CPC ini?\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The detected fraction depends on the check's support at the error location. If the propagated check acts on $w$ of the $n$ data qubits there, it anti-commutes with two of $\\{X,Y,Z\\}$ on each supported qubit and commutes with all three on the others. This sweep therefore detects $2w$ of the $3n$ single-qubit Pauli faults, a fraction $2w/(3n)$. Read the support and detected count from the output above; they change with the payload and the chosen insertion point. The support at this slice is part of the check's detection region, the spacetime wires reached by its back-cumulant ([Martiel & Javadi-Abhari, Supp. III-A](https://arxiv.org/abs/2504.15725)).\n"
msgstr "Pecahan yang dikesan bergantung pada sokongan semakan pada lokasi ralat. Jika semakan yang dirambatkan bertindak pada $w$ daripada $n$ qubit data di situ, ia berantikalis tukar tertib dengan dua daripada $\\{X,Y,Z\\}$ pada setiap qubit yang disokong dan berkalis tukar tertib dengan ketiga-tiganya pada yang lain. Sapuan ini oleh itu mengesan $2w$ daripada $3n$ kerosakan Pauli qubit tunggal, iaitu pecahan $2w/(3n)$. Baca sokongan dan kiraan yang dikesan daripada keluaran di atas; ia berubah mengikut muatan dan titik sisipan yang dipilih. Sokongan pada hirisan ini merupakan sebahagian daripada kawasan pengesanan semakan, iaitu wayar ruang-masa yang dicapai oleh kumulan belakangnya ([Martiel & Javadi-Abhari, Supp. III-A](https://arxiv.org/abs/2504.15725)).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Checks with larger support at this slice catch a larger fraction of this sweep. Additional check pairs at different positions can extend coverage, but each brings its own $L$ operator. The detection rule as stated covers Pauli errors; a general error is a combination of Paulis, and a coherent or non-unitary error is caught only with the probability carried by the components that anti-commute with the check.\n"
msgstr "Semakan dengan sokongan lebih besar pada hirisan ini menangkap pecahan sapuan ini yang lebih besar. Pasangan semakan tambahan pada kedudukan berbeza boleh meluaskan liputan, tetapi setiap satu membawa operator $L$ tersendiri. Peraturan pengesanan seperti yang dinyatakan meliputi ralat Pauli; ralat am ialah gabungan Pauli, dan ralat koheren atau bukan unitari hanya ditangkap dengan kebarangkalian yang dibawa oleh komponen yang berantikalis tukar tertib dengan semakan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "2.3.2 One-sided CPC: reading $R$ from the data {#232-one-sided-cpc-reading-r-from-the-data}"
msgstr "2.3.2 CPC satu-sisi: membaca $R$ daripada data {#232-one-sided-cpc-reading-r-from-the-data}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The compiled resource counts in Section 2.2.1 show why a valid CPC can still be expensive: one ancilla must reach the supports of both $L$ and $R$. Their weights count the controlled-Pauli couplings, while hardware connectivity and routing determine the additional cost. A lower-weight check need not give a shallower compiled circuit.\n"
msgstr "Kiraan sumber terkompil dalam Bahagian 2.2.1 menunjukkan mengapa CPC yang sah masih boleh mahal: satu ancilla mesti mencapai sokongan kedua-dua $L$ dan $R$. Pemberat mereka mengira gandingan Pauli terkawal, manakala kesambungan perkakasan dan penghalaan menentukan kos tambahan. Semakan berpemberat lebih rendah tidak semestinya menghasilkan litar terkompil yang lebih cetek.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In Section 2.5 of their [paper](https://arxiv.org/abs/2212.03937), van den Berg et al. reduce that cost by moving the check qubit along a line and combining each controlled-Pauli gate with the following swap. Their construction shows why designing checks together with qubit motion can be cheaper than relying on a generic router. Their one-sided construction also removes controlled-$R$ gates by evaluating a Z-type $R$ from the final data bits; we illustrate that option below.\n"
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Implementation detail: phase compensation\">\n"
msgstr ""
"Dalam Bahagian 2.5 [kertas](https://arxiv.org/abs/2212.03937) mereka, van den Berg et al. mengurangkan kos itu dengan menggerakkan qubit semakan di sepanjang garisan dan menggabungkan setiap gate Pauli terkawal dengan pertukaran (swap) yang mengikutinya. Binaan mereka menunjukkan mengapa mereka bentuk semakan bersama pergerakan qubit boleh lebih murah daripada bergantung pada penghala generik. Binaan satu-sisi mereka juga menyingkirkan gate $R$ terkawal dengan menilai $R$ jenis-Z daripada bit data akhir; kita menggambarkan pilihan itu di bawah.\n"
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Butiran pelaksanaan: pampasan fasa\">\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`Pauli.phase` from Qiskit stores an overall factor $(-i)^k$. The `apply_controlled_paulis` helper implements the tensor factors but omits that phase. Under control it becomes a relative phase on the ancilla, so we restore it with $S^\\dagger$, $Z$, or $S$ for exponents 1, 2, or 3. For a CPC pair, use `L.phase + R.phase` modulo four. The one-sided example below uses `L.phase` alone. See [Martiel & Javadi-Abhari, Supplementary Information §II-C and Fig. S3](https://arxiv.org/abs/2504.15725).\n"
msgstr "`Pauli.phase` daripada Qiskit menyimpan faktor keseluruhan $(-i)^k$. Pembantu `apply_controlled_paulis` melaksanakan faktor tensor tetapi mengabaikan fasa itu. Di bawah kawalan ia menjadi fasa relatif pada ancilla, jadi kita memulihkannya dengan $S^\\dagger$, $Z$, atau $S$ untuk eksponen 1, 2, atau 3. Bagi pasangan CPC, gunakan `L.phase + R.phase` modulo empat. Contoh satu-sisi di bawah hanya menggunakan `L.phase`. Lihat [Martiel & Javadi-Abhari, Supplementary Information §II-C and Fig. S3](https://arxiv.org/abs/2504.15725).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"</Accordion>\n"
"**One-sided checks**\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A CPC pair can also compare an ancilla result with the final data bits. As in [van den Berg et al.](https://arxiv.org/abs/2212.03937), implement $L = U^\\dagger R U$ with controlled gates and evaluate $R$ classically when it is diagonal in the measurement basis. For the $R=Z_8Z_9$ example from [Section 2.2](#coherent), the syndrome is the input-check bit XOR the two output bits. Ideal shots give zero, while an $X$ fault on qubit 8 after the payload flips that syndrome.\n"
msgstr "Pasangan CPC juga boleh membandingkan keputusan ancilla dengan bit data akhir. Seperti dalam [van den Berg et al.](https://arxiv.org/abs/2212.03937), laksanakan $L = U^\\dagger R U$ dengan gate terkawal dan nilai $R$ secara klasik apabila ia pepenjuru dalam asas pengukuran. Bagi contoh $R=Z_8Z_9$ daripada [Bahagian 2.2](#coherent), sindrom ialah bit semakan masukan XOR kedua-dua bit keluaran. Tembakan ideal memberikan sifar, manakala kerosakan $X$ pada qubit 8 selepas muatan membalikkan sindrom itu.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The cell below reuses `apply_controlled_paulis` on the same payload, with no inverse and no controlled-$R$ gates. This preserves the ideal final Z-basis statistics, although measuring $L$ can change the underlying data state. It illustrates the check identity, rather than benchmarking its hardware benefit.\n"
msgstr "Sel di bawah menggunakan semula `apply_controlled_paulis` pada muatan yang sama, tanpa songsangan dan tanpa gate $R$ terkawal. Ini mengekalkan statistik asas-Z akhir yang ideal, walaupun mengukur $L$ boleh mengubah keadaan data yang mendasari. Ia menggambarkan identiti semakan, dan bukannya menanda aras manfaat perkakasannya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Measuring $L$ on an ancilla is a projective measurement of the payload. Unless $L$ is a stabilizer of the state at that point, the measurement collapses the state onto a random $\\pm 1$ eigenspace of $L$. The eigenvalue is then faithfully carried to $R$ (which is why the XOR still passes), but the payload that continues through the circuit is no longer the state the computation prepared. In this one-sided construction, the data state can change while the ideal statistics in the chosen measurement basis remain unchanged.\n"
msgstr "Mengukur $L$ pada ancilla ialah pengukuran proyektif ke atas muatan. Melainkan $L$ ialah penstabil bagi keadaan pada titik itu, pengukuran meruntuhkan keadaan ke ruang eigen $\\pm 1$ rawak bagi $L$. Nilai eigen itu kemudian dibawa dengan setia kepada $R$ (itulah sebabnya XOR masih lulus), tetapi muatan yang diteruskan melalui litar tidak lagi merupakan keadaan yang disediakan oleh pengiraan. Dalam binaan satu-sisi ini, keadaan data boleh berubah sementara statistik ideal dalam asas pengukuran yang dipilih kekal tidak berubah.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Section 2.3.3 takes a different simplification of the CPC identity, as follows: choose $L$ to be a known input stabilizer, so its physical check can be omitted. This leads to an interior stabilizer check.\n"
msgstr "Bahagian 2.3.3 mengambil penyederhanaan berbeza bagi identiti CPC, seperti berikut: pilih $L$ sebagai penstabil masukan yang diketahui, supaya semakan fizikalnya boleh ditinggalkan. Ini membawa kepada semakan penstabil dalaman.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "2.3.3 From CPC to spacetime codes: placing checks where they work {#233-from-cpc-to-spacetime-codes-placing-checks-where-they-work}"
msgstr "2.3.3 Daripada CPC kepada kod ruang-masa: meletakkan semakan di tempat ia berfungsi {#233-from-cpc-to-spacetime-codes-placing-checks-where-they-work}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Two-sided CPC compares $L$ at the input with $R$ at the output. If $L$ is a known input stabilizer, its value supplies the reference and its physical check can be omitted, leaving a right-only check. The input $|0\\rangle^{\\otimes n}$ is stabilized by any product of $Z$ operators, such as $Z_j$ or the all-$Z$ operator. Choose $L=Z_j$ and propagate it forward through the payload:\n"
msgstr "CPC dua-sisi membandingkan $L$ pada masukan dengan $R$ pada keluaran. Jika $L$ ialah penstabil masukan yang diketahui, nilainya menyediakan rujukan dan semakan fizikalnya boleh ditinggalkan, menyisakan semakan kanan-sahaja. Masukan $|0\\rangle^{\\otimes n}$ distabilkan oleh sebarang hasil darab operator $Z$, seperti $Z_j$ atau operator semua-$Z$. Pilih $L=Z_j$ dan rambatkannya ke hadapan melalui muatan:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "$$R_j=U Z_j U^\\dagger,\\qquad R_j\\, U|0\\rangle^{\\otimes n}=U|0\\rangle^{\\otimes n}.$$\n"
msgstr "$$R_j=U Z_j U^\\dagger,\\qquad R_j\\, U|0\\rangle^{\\otimes n}=U|0\\rangle^{\\otimes n}.$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Measuring $R_j$ at the output therefore gives $+1$ ideally. An arbitrary CPC choice of $R$ need not have a known value, so dropping its partner can produce random outcomes. Clifford propagation keeps each $R_j$ a single Pauli, and the circuit sets its type and support. Finding $R_j$ means computing classically what the payload does to $Z_j$: efficient at any depth for our Clifford payload, but in a general circuit with non-Clifford gates typically cheap only through the first layers. A right-only check therefore gives a general computation a solid start, not a way around classical simulation.\n"
msgstr "Mengukur $R_j$ pada keluaran oleh itu memberikan $+1$ secara ideal. Pilihan $R$ CPC sewenang-wenangnya tidak semestinya mempunyai nilai yang diketahui, jadi membuang pasangannya boleh menghasilkan keputusan rawak. Perambatan Clifford mengekalkan setiap $R_j$ sebagai satu Pauli, dan litar menetapkan jenis dan sokongannya. Mencari $R_j$ bermakna mengira secara klasik apa yang dilakukan muatan kepada $Z_j$: cekap pada sebarang kedalaman untuk muatan Clifford kita, tetapi dalam litar am dengan gate bukan Clifford ia lazimnya murah hanya melalui beberapa lapisan pertama. Semakan kanan-sahaja oleh itu memberikan permulaan yang kukuh kepada pengiraan am, bukan cara mengelak simulasi klasik.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Check your understanding {#check-your-understanding-5}"
msgstr "Semak kefahaman anda {#check-your-understanding-5}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Why not measure an arbitrary CPC pair $L$ and $R$ separately, then XOR their outcomes?\n"
msgstr "Mengapa tidak mengukur pasangan CPC sewenang-wenangnya $L$ dan $R$ secara berasingan, kemudian XOR keputusan mereka?\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The XOR agrees ideally, but measuring $L$ can project the data onto a random eigenstate and disrupt later coherent computation. The coherent CPC sandwich avoids revealing either individual value. Measuring a known stabilizer is harmless ideally, while reconstructing a partner from compatible final data measurements, as above, preserves those measurement statistics.\n"
msgstr "XOR itu sepakat secara ideal, tetapi mengukur $L$ boleh memproyeksikan data ke keadaan eigen rawak dan mengganggu pengiraan koheren seterusnya. Sandwic CPC koheren mengelak pendedahan mana-mana nilai individu. Mengukur penstabil yang diketahui tidak berbahaya secara ideal, manakala membina semula pasangan daripada pengukuran data akhir yang serasi, seperti di atas, mengekalkan statistik pengukuran tersebut.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"</Accordion>\n"
"For each $R_j$, prepare an ancilla in $|+\\rangle$, apply its controlled-Pauli factors and any sign correction, then measure in the $X$ basis (H followed by a computational-basis measurement). The ideal result is bit `0`, corresponding to eigenvalue $+1$.\n"
msgstr ""
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"</Accordion>\n"
"Bagi setiap $R_j$, sediakan ancilla dalam $|+\\rangle$, kenakan faktor Pauli terkawalnya dan sebarang pembetulan tanda, kemudian ukur dalam asas $X$ (H diikuti pengukuran asas pengiraan). Keputusan ideal ialah bit `0`, sepadan dengan nilai eigen $+1$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The next cell measures all 20 generators to illustrate the routing cost; using a subset also gives valid right-only checks. The 20 data qubits and 20 ancillas sit on one line, as on a device with only nearest-neighbor couplers. Each ancilla must meet every data qubit in the support of its $R_j$, so the ancillas are swapped through the data line. A controlled-Pauli fused with the swap that follows it costs two CZ gates [van den Berg et al.](https://arxiv.org/abs/2212.03937), and a swap past a data qubit outside the support still costs three. The cell checks that no ancilla fires without noise, compares CZ counts, and draws the circuit. The payload sits left of the barrier, and the diamond of SWAP gates carries the ancillas up through the data line.\n"
msgstr "Sel seterusnya mengukur kesemua 20 penjana untuk menggambarkan kos penghalaan; menggunakan subset juga memberikan semakan kanan-sahaja yang sah. 20 qubit data dan 20 ancilla terletak pada satu garisan, seperti pada peranti dengan penggandingan jiran terdekat sahaja. Setiap ancilla mesti bertemu setiap qubit data dalam sokongan $R_j$ nya, jadi ancilla ditukar melalui garisan data. Pauli terkawal yang digabungkan dengan pertukaran yang mengikutinya berharga dua gate CZ [van den Berg et al.](https://arxiv.org/abs/2212.03937), dan pertukaran melepasi qubit data di luar sokongan masih berharga tiga. Sel ini menyemak bahawa tiada ancilla menyala tanpa hingar, membandingkan kiraan CZ, dan melukis litar. Muatan terletak di sebelah kiri penghalang, dan berlian gate SWAP membawa ancilla ke atas melalui garisan data.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/tools-for-quantum-advantage/error-correction-i/extracted-outputs/4c2e2a1e-1.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/tools-for-quantum-advantage/error-correction-i/extracted-outputs/4c2e2a1e-1.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Every check in this circuit is valid, and each ancilla measures one stabilizer, so each catches the faults that anti-commute with its $R_j$. The cost is the problem. In this layout, reaching the supports takes 400 swaps, and even with each controlled-Pauli fused into a swap, the checks need more than twenty times as many CZ gates as the payload they protect. Those gates and the waiting ancillas add errors of their own, so on hardware the added noise can easily outweigh what the checks detect. These counts describe this routing construction, not a minimum: placement and check support determine the routing cost on the nearest-neighbor line.\n"
"A check need not occupy one time slice. A *wire* $w$ is a qubit between two layers. Let $A_w$ be the circuit prefix up to that wire. The Pauli's back-propagator is $B(P,w)=A_w^\\dagger P A_w$. For input $|0\\rangle^{\\otimes n}$, couplings in time order $1,\\ldots,m$ form a valid check when:\n"
msgstr ""
"Setiap semakan dalam litar ini sah, dan setiap ancilla mengukur satu penstabil, jadi setiap satu menangkap kerosakan yang berantikalis tukar tertib dengan $R_j$ nya. Kosnya yang menjadi masalah. Dalam susun atur ini, mencapai sokongan memerlukan 400 swap, dan walaupun setiap Pauli terkawal digabungkan ke dalam swap, semakan memerlukan lebih daripada dua puluh kali ganda gate CZ berbanding muatan yang dilindunginya. Gate-gate itu dan ancilla yang menunggu menambah ralat sendiri, jadi pada perkakasan hingar tambahan itu mudah mengatasi apa yang dikesan oleh semakan. Kiraan ini menerangkan binaan penghalaan ini, bukan minimum: penempatan dan sokongan semakan menentukan kos penghalaan pada garisan jiran terdekat.\n"
"Semakan tidak perlu menduduki satu hirisan masa. *Wayar* $w$ ialah qubit di antara dua lapisan. Biar $A_w$ ialah awalan litar sehingga wayar itu. Perambat-belakang Pauli ialah $B(P,w)=A_w^\\dagger P A_w$. Untuk masukan $|0\\rangle^{\\otimes n}$, gandingan mengikut tertib masa $1,\\ldots,m$ membentuk semakan yang sah apabila:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "$$B(P_m,w_m)\\cdots B(P_1,w_1)=i^\\phi S,\\qquad S\\in\\langle Z_0,\\ldots,Z_{n-1}\\rangle.$$\n"
msgstr "$$B(P_m,w_m)\\cdots B(P_1,w_1)=i^\\phi S,\\qquad S\\in\\langle Z_0,\\ldots,Z_{n-1}\\rangle.$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Prepare the ancilla in $|+\\rangle$, apply each controlled Pauli at its wire, cancel the accumulated phase $i^\\phi$ on the ancilla, and measure it in the $X$ basis ([Martiel & Javadi-Abhari, Eq. 2](https://arxiv.org/abs/2504.15725)). We keep every coupling on one neighboring data qubit to avoid routing while allowing support at different times.\n"
"<span id=\"paulice\"></span>\n"
msgstr ""
"Sediakan ancilla dalam $|+\\rangle$, kenakan setiap Pauli terkawal pada wayarnya, batalkan fasa terkumpul $i^\\phi$ pada ancilla, dan ukurnya dalam asas $X$ ([Martiel & Javadi-Abhari, Eq. 2](https://arxiv.org/abs/2504.15725)). Kita mengekalkan setiap gandingan pada satu qubit data jiran untuk mengelak penghalaan sambil membenarkan sokongan pada masa yang berbeza.\n"
"<span id=\"paulice\"></span>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "2.4 Spacetime checks with Paulice {#24-spacetime-checks-with-paulice}"
msgstr "2.4 Semakan ruang-masa dengan Paulice {#24-spacetime-checks-with-paulice}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The right-only example in Section 2.3.3 showed that removing $L$ does not eliminate routing. Each ancilla still has to reach the support of its output stabilizer. The local spacetime construction introduced above avoids this routing by placing an ancilla's couplings at different times on a single neighboring data wire.\n"
msgstr "Contoh kanan-sahaja dalam Bahagian 2.3.3 menunjukkan bahawa membuang $L$ tidak menghapuskan penghalaan. Setiap ancilla masih perlu mencapai sokongan penstabil keluarannya. Binaan ruang-masa setempat yang diperkenalkan di atas mengelak penghalaan ini dengan meletakkan gandingan ancilla pada masa yang berbeza pada satu wayar data jiran.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "[Qiskit Paulice](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/addons/qiskit-addon-paulice) automates this search for a given circuit and measurement. Each data qubit with a free neighbor on the device can be a *target*, and that neighbor becomes its check ancilla. With `method=\"windowed\"`, as in the [IBM Quantum spacetime-code tutorial](/tutorials/spacetime-codes), `add_pauli_checks` searches windows of couplings along each target's wire. A check's syndrome is the XOR of its ancilla bit and, where the search needs them, final data bits listed in `check_support`. Data bits are read out anyway, so that part of a check costs no gates.\n"
msgstr "[Qiskit Paulice](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/addons/qiskit-addon-paulice) mengautomasikan carian ini untuk litar dan pengukuran tertentu. Setiap qubit data dengan jiran bebas pada peranti boleh menjadi *sasaran*, dan jiran itu menjadi ancilla semakannya. Dengan `method=\"windowed\"`, seperti dalam [tutorial kod ruang-masa IBM Quantum](/tutorials/spacetime-codes), `add_pauli_checks` mencari tetingkap gandingan di sepanjang wayar setiap sasaran. Sindrom sesuatu semakan ialah XOR bit ancilla dan, apabila carian memerlukannya, bit data akhir yang disenaraikan dalam `check_support`. Bit data dibaca juga, jadi bahagian semakan itu tidak memerlukan gate.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Paulice scores checks with *gamma*: under a noise model built from the device calibration, it estimates the quasi-probability cost of cancelling the noise the checks leave undetected within the lightcone of the measurement, and lower is better. Gamma is a model score, distinct from the acceptance overhead $1/A$ of Part 1. Checks are committed one target at a time, and the search returns the circuit after each commitment. The model takes the error of each data-line coupler from the calibration but gives the couplers a check adds a typical rate, so it would not notice a faulty one; we therefore keep only target-ancilla pairs with calibrated coupler error below 0.05 and ancilla readout error below 0.1.\n"
msgstr "Paulice menilai semakan dengan *gamma*: di bawah model hingar yang dibina daripada penentukuran peranti, ia menganggarkan kos kuasi-kebarangkalian untuk membatalkan hingar yang dibiarkan tidak dikesan oleh semakan dalam kon cahaya pengukuran, dan nilai lebih rendah adalah lebih baik. Gamma ialah skor model, berbeza daripada overhed penerimaan $1/A$ dalam Bahagian 1. Semakan dikomit satu sasaran pada satu masa, dan carian memulangkan litar selepas setiap komitmen. Model mengambil ralat setiap penggandingan talian data daripada penentukuran tetapi memberikan kadar lazim kepada penggandingan yang ditambah oleh semakan, jadi ia tidak akan menyedari penggandingan yang rosak; oleh itu kita hanya mengekalkan pasangan sasaran-ancilla dengan ralat penggandingan tertentukur di bawah 0.05 dan ralat bacaan ancilla di bawah 0.1.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For Sections [2.4](#paulice)-[2.5](#hardware-experiment), we extend the same 20-qubit circuit construction from five to ten CZ layers, keeping the generator and random seed fixed. The deeper payload gives errors more opportunities to accumulate and spread, so that we can test whether post-selection can outweigh the added check cost. We run this payload forward, without its inverse, and sample ten signed stabilizers of its ideal output. The stabilizers and Paulice checks are computed for this deeper circuit. We select one physical data line and reuse it for every unchecked and checked circuit. The first sampled stabilizer $G_0$ supplies the measurement for the placement comparison below, and [Section 2.5](#hardware-experiment) repeats the search for each stabilizer. We first recall how a check's support moves backward through the gates.\n"
"The idea is to take a check operator and pull it backward through the circuit, one gate at a time. At each layer, we record which qubits the operator touches; together, these qubits and layers form the check's detection region. To do this, we need to know how Pauli operators transform when they pass through a gate in reverse. For any Clifford gate, the result is always another Pauli, which is what makes the tracking exact. Our payload uses CZ gates and single-qubit Clifford gates. A CZ, for example, maps:\n"
msgstr ""
"Untuk Bahagian [2.4](#paulice)-[2.5](#hardware-experiment), kami memanjangkan pembinaan litar 20-qubit yang sama daripada lima kepada sepuluh lapisan CZ, dengan penjana dan benih rawak dikekalkan. Muatan yang lebih dalam memberi lebih banyak peluang kepada ralat untuk terkumpul dan merebak, supaya kami dapat menguji sama ada pasca-pemilihan boleh mengatasi kos semakan tambahan. Kami menjalankan muatan ini ke hadapan, tanpa songsangannya, dan mensampel sepuluh penstabil bertanda bagi outputnya yang ideal. Penstabil dan semakan Paulice dikira untuk litar yang lebih dalam ini. Kami memilih satu talian data fizikal dan menggunakannya semula untuk setiap litar tanpa semakan dan dengan semakan. Penstabil pertama yang disampel $G_0$ membekalkan pengukuran untuk perbandingan penempatan di bawah, dan [Bahagian 2.5](#hardware-experiment) mengulangi carian untuk setiap penstabil. Kita mulakan dengan mengingat semula bagaimana sokongan sesuatu semakan bergerak ke belakang melalui gate.\n"
"Idea asasnya ialah mengambil operator semakan dan menariknya ke belakang melalui litar, satu gate pada satu masa. Pada setiap lapisan, kami merekodkan qubit yang disentuh oleh operator; qubit dan lapisan ini bersama-sama membentuk kawasan pengesanan semakan. Untuk melakukannya, kita perlu tahu bagaimana operator Pauli berubah apabila melalui sesuatu gate secara terbalik. Bagi mana-mana gate Clifford, hasilnya sentiasa operator Pauli yang lain, dan inilah yang menjadikan penjejakan itu tepat. Muatan kami menggunakan gate CZ dan gate Clifford satu-qubit. Sebagai contoh, CZ memetakan:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "$$X_a \\xrightarrow{\\text{CZ}(a, b)} X_a Z_b,$$\n"
msgstr "$$X_a \\xrightarrow{\\text{CZ}(a, b)} X_a Z_b,$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "so an $X$ in a check's support picks up a $Z$ on the partner qubit, while a $Z$ passes through unchanged. Each two-qubit layer can add qubits to the support or remove them, so the detection region changes shape as it moves backward in time. The rules for CNOT and CZ are collected below.\n"
msgstr "jadi $X$ dalam sokongan sesuatu semakan mendapat $Z$ pada qubit pasangannya, manakala $Z$ melaluinya tanpa berubah. Setiap lapisan dua-qubit boleh menambah qubit ke dalam sokongan atau mengeluarkannya, jadi kawasan pengesanan berubah bentuk apabila bergerak ke belakang dalam masa. Peraturan untuk CNOT dan CZ dihimpunkan di bawah.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Conjugation rules for two-qubit gates, and what single-qubit gates do\">\n"
msgstr ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Peraturan konjugasi untuk gate dua-qubit, dan kesan gate satu-qubit\">\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The conjugation $U^\\dagger P U$ pulls a check operator $P$ at the output of a gate back to its input. Forward propagation of an error instead uses $U P U^\\dagger$. For Clifford gates, the result is always another Pauli.\n"
msgstr "Konjugasi $U^\\dagger P U$ menarik operator semakan $P$ pada output sesuatu gate kembali ke inputnya. Perambatan ke hadapan bagi sesuatu ralat pula menggunakan $U P U^\\dagger$. Bagi gate Clifford, hasilnya sentiasa operator Pauli yang lain.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Single-qubit gates (H, S, and so on) can change the type of error on a wire (for example, $X \\leftrightarrow Z$ through H) but cannot spread it to another qubit. Only two-qubit entangling gates move errors between wires, which is why detection regions grow only at entangling layers.\n"
msgstr "Gate satu-qubit (H, S, dan sebagainya) boleh mengubah jenis ralat pada sesuatu wayar (contohnya, $X \\leftrightarrow Z$ melalui H) tetapi tidak boleh menyebarkannya ke qubit lain. Hanya gate belitan dua-qubit yang memindahkan ralat antara wayar, itulah sebabnya kawasan pengesanan hanya membesar pada lapisan belitan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "*CNOT* (control $c$, target $t$), an *asymmetric* gate:\n"
msgstr "*CNOT* (kawalan $c$, sasaran $t$), gate yang *tidak simetri*:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "$$X_c \\mapsto X_c X_t, \\quad Z_c \\mapsto Z_c, \\quad X_t \\mapsto X_t, \\quad Z_t \\mapsto Z_c Z_t.$$\n"
msgstr "$$X_c \\mapsto X_c X_t, \\quad Z_c \\mapsto Z_c, \\quad X_t \\mapsto X_t, \\quad Z_t \\mapsto Z_c Z_t.$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "CNOT does \"if control is 1, flip target.\" This asymmetry determines how different errors propagate:\n"
msgstr "CNOT melakukan \"jika kawalan ialah 1, balikkan sasaran.\" Ketaksimetrian ini menentukan bagaimana ralat yang berbeza merambat:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Bit-flips ($X$) travel *control → target*. An $X$ on the control changes whether the target gets flipped, so the error spreads to the target ($X_c \\mapsto X_c X_t$). An $X$ on the target flips it regardless of the control, so it stays put ($X_t \\mapsto X_t$).\n"
msgstr "Pembalikan bit ($X$) bergerak *kawalan → sasaran*. $X$ pada kawalan mengubah sama ada sasaran dibalikkan, jadi ralat merebak ke sasaran ($X_c \\mapsto X_c X_t$). $X$ pada sasaran membalikkannya tanpa mengira kawalan, jadi ia kekal di tempatnya ($X_t \\mapsto X_t$).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Phase-flips ($Z$) travel *target → control*. CNOT makes the target's value depend on the control ($|c,t\\rangle \\to |c, c \\oplus t\\rangle$), so a phase applied to the target effectively becomes conditional on the control's value, kicking a phase back to the control. This is the same *phase kickback* mechanism used in algorithms like Deutsch-Jozsa and quantum phase estimation. The result is $Z_t \\mapsto Z_c Z_t$. Meanwhile $Z$ on the control does not involve the target at all, so $Z_c \\mapsto Z_c$.\n"
msgstr "Pembalikan fasa ($Z$) bergerak *sasaran → kawalan*. CNOT menjadikan nilai sasaran bergantung pada kawalan ($|c,t\\rangle \\to |c, c \\oplus t\\rangle$), jadi fasa yang dikenakan pada sasaran secara berkesan menjadi bersyarat pada nilai kawalan, lalu menendang fasa kembali ke kawalan. Ini ialah mekanisme *phase kickback* yang sama yang digunakan dalam algoritma seperti Deutsch-Jozsa dan penganggaran fasa kuantum. Hasilnya ialah $Z_t \\mapsto Z_c Z_t$. Sementara itu, $Z$ pada kawalan langsung tidak melibatkan sasaran, jadi $Z_c \\mapsto Z_c$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In short: *bit-flips flow forward* (control → target), *phase-flips flow backward* (target → control). This directional asymmetry is why backward propagation of $Z$-type checks through a CNOT chain fans out from target toward controls.\n"
msgstr "Ringkasnya: *pembalikan bit mengalir ke hadapan* (kawalan → sasaran), *pembalikan fasa mengalir ke belakang* (sasaran → kawalan). Ketaksimetrian arah ini menjelaskan mengapa perambatan ke belakang bagi semakan jenis $Z$ melalui rantaian CNOT bercabang dari sasaran ke arah kawalan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "*CZ* (qubits $a$, $b$), a *symmetric* gate:\n"
msgstr "*CZ* (qubit $a$, $b$), gate yang *simetri*:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "$$X_a \\mapsto X_a Z_b, \\quad Z_a \\mapsto Z_a, \\quad X_b \\mapsto Z_a X_b, \\quad Z_b \\mapsto Z_b.$$\n"
msgstr "$$X_a \\mapsto X_a Z_b, \\quad Z_a \\mapsto Z_a, \\quad X_b \\mapsto Z_a X_b, \\quad Z_b \\mapsto Z_b.$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Unlike CNOT, CZ treats both qubits identically; there is no \"control\" or \"target.\" A bit-flip on either qubit picks up a phase-flip on the other. Phase-flips pass through unchanged on both sides. The symmetry means error propagation looks the same from either direction.\n"
msgstr "Tidak seperti CNOT, CZ memperlakukan kedua-dua qubit secara sama; tiada \"kawalan\" atau \"sasaran.\" Pembalikan bit pada mana-mana qubit mendapat pembalikan fasa pada yang satu lagi. Pembalikan fasa melalui kedua-dua belah tanpa berubah. Kesimetrian ini bermakna perambatan ralat kelihatan sama dari mana-mana arah.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The pattern to remember: entangling gates *spread* errors. A single-qubit error before the gate can become a two-qubit error after it. This is both the source of the problem (errors propagate through the circuit) and the basis of detection (a check's sensitivity propagates the same way).\n"
msgstr "Corak yang perlu diingat: gate belitan *menyebarkan* ralat. Ralat satu-qubit sebelum gate boleh menjadi ralat dua-qubit selepasnya. Ini ialah punca masalah (ralat merambat melalui litar) dan juga asas pengesanan (kepekaan sesuatu semakan merambat dengan cara yang sama).\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/tools-for-quantum-advantage/error-correction-i/extracted-outputs/bed76e8d-1.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/tools-for-quantum-advantage/error-correction-i/extracted-outputs/bed76e8d-1.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The first table lists one check per target. Each check couples its ancilla to the target wire at a few points along the payload, the layers shown in the table, and its syndrome might add final data bits. The second table follows the search as it commits checks. Compare the change in gamma and the added two-qubit gates at each step. The targets are ordered by their single-check scores, but overlapping detection regions and noise from added gates mean that the largest improvement need not come first, and a committed check can raise gamma. The device map shows data qubits in green, committed check ancillas in orange, and unused qubits in gray. Each check ancilla is next to its target, so the couplings need no routing.\n"
"Each check covers the spacetime region its couplings and syndrome bits reach by back-propagation, as in Section 2.3.3. Coverage is not the whole story, however. Each check adds gates, and gamma weighs the detected noise against the noise those gates bring. Gamma depends on the noise model and on the chosen measurement, so a lower gamma is a search preference, not a guarantee of a better hardware result, and it is not an acceptance rate or a measured fidelity.\n"
msgstr ""
"Jadual pertama menyenaraikan satu semakan bagi setiap sasaran. Setiap semakan menggandingkan ancilla-nya kepada wayar sasaran pada beberapa titik di sepanjang muatan, iaitu lapisan yang ditunjukkan dalam jadual, dan sindromnya mungkin menambah bit data akhir. Jadual kedua mengikuti carian apabila ia melakukan komit semakan. Bandingkan perubahan gamma dan gate dua-qubit tambahan pada setiap langkah. Sasaran disusun mengikut skor semakan tunggal masing-masing, tetapi kawasan pengesanan yang bertindih dan hingar daripada gate tambahan bermakna peningkatan terbesar tidak semestinya datang dahulu, dan semakan yang telah dikomit boleh menaikkan gamma. Peta peranti menunjukkan qubit data dalam warna hijau, ancilla semakan yang dikomit dalam oren, dan qubit yang tidak digunakan dalam kelabu. Setiap ancilla semakan berada bersebelahan sasarannya, jadi gandingan tidak memerlukan penghalaan.\n"
"Setiap semakan meliputi kawasan ruang-masa yang dicapai oleh gandingan dan bit sindromnya melalui perambatan ke belakang, seperti dalam Bahagian 2.3.3. Namun, liputan bukan keseluruhan ceritanya. Setiap semakan menambah gate, dan gamma menimbang hingar yang dikesan berbanding hingar yang dibawa oleh gate tersebut. Gamma bergantung pada model hingar dan pada pengukuran yang dipilih, jadi gamma yang lebih rendah ialah keutamaan carian, bukan jaminan hasil perkakasan yang lebih baik, dan ia bukan kadar penerimaan atau fideliti yang diukur.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The checks also depend on the measured observable. Here they were chosen for $G_0$. [Section 2.5](#hardware-experiment) repeats the search for every sampled stabilizer and runs the resulting circuits on hardware.\n"
msgstr "Semakan juga bergantung pada observabel yang diukur. Di sini ia dipilih untuk $G_0$. [Bahagian 2.5](#hardware-experiment) mengulangi carian untuk setiap penstabil yang disampel dan menjalankan litar yang terhasil pada perkakasan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Check your understanding {#check-your-understanding-6}"
msgstr "Semak kefahaman anda {#check-your-understanding-6}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A check has a detection region covering some set of spacetime locations. Does this mean it catches every error at those locations?\n"
msgstr "Sesuatu semakan mempunyai kawasan pengesanan yang meliputi satu set lokasi ruang-masa. Adakah ini bermakna ia menangkap setiap ralat pada lokasi tersebut?\n"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Not every type. At each location in the detection region, the check detects errors that anti-commute with its propagated support there; errors that commute pass through undetected. For one check, the propagated support at a location is a single Pauli, so the check catches two of $X$, $Y$, and $Z$ there and misses the third. This is why a single check has weaknesses even within its own detection region, and why complementary checks with different Pauli types or placements are needed for broader protection.\n"
msgstr "Tidak semua jenis. Pada setiap lokasi dalam kawasan pengesanan, semakan mengesan ralat yang antikalis tukar tertib dengan sokongan terrambatnya di situ; ralat yang kalis tukar tertib melepasinya tanpa dikesan. Bagi satu semakan, sokongan terrambat pada sesuatu lokasi ialah satu Pauli, jadi semakan menangkap dua daripada $X$, $Y$, dan $Z$ di situ dan terlepas yang ketiga. Inilah sebabnya satu semakan mempunyai kelemahan walaupun dalam kawasan pengesanannya sendiri, dan mengapa semakan pelengkap dengan jenis atau penempatan Pauli yang berbeza diperlukan untuk perlindungan yang lebih luas.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"</Accordion>\n"
"<span id=\"hardware-experiment\"></span>\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "2.5 Hardware experiment: spacetime checks on the payload {#25-hardware-experiment-spacetime-checks-on-the-payload}"
msgstr "2.5 Eksperimen perkakasan: semakan ruang-masa pada muatan {#25-hardware-experiment-spacetime-checks-on-the-payload}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "[Section 2.4](#paulice) used a device-based noise model to select and score checks. We now test on hardware whether post-selection brings the measured observables closer to their ideal values, and how many shots that improvement costs. Using the same ten-layer payload and fixed data line, we compare an unchecked baseline with an increasing number of checks. Following the [spacetime-code tutorial](/tutorials/spacetime-codes), we repeat the search for each sampled stabilizer and compare raw and post-selected expectation values alongside acceptance.\n"
msgstr "[Bahagian 2.4](#paulice) menggunakan model hingar berasaskan peranti untuk memilih dan menskor semakan. Kini kami menguji pada perkakasan sama ada pasca-pemilihan membawa observabel yang diukur lebih dekat kepada nilai idealnya, dan berapa banyak shot yang diperlukan untuk peningkatan itu. Dengan muatan sepuluh lapisan yang sama dan talian data tetap, kami membandingkan garis dasar tanpa semakan dengan bilangan semakan yang semakin meningkat. Mengikut [tutorial kod ruang-masa](/tutorials/spacetime-codes), kami mengulangi carian untuk setiap penstabil yang disampel dan membandingkan nilai jangkaan mentah dan pasca-pilih bersama-sama dengan kadar penerimaan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Why sampled stabilizers? {#why-sampled-stabilizers}"
msgstr "Mengapa penstabil yang disampel? {#why-sampled-stabilizers}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The payload prepares a stabilizer state $|\\psi\\rangle = U|0\\rangle^{\\otimes n}$, and its projector is the average of the $2^n$ signed elements of its stabilizer group, $|\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi| = 2^{-n} \\sum_G G$. The fidelity $\\langle\\psi|\\rho|\\psi\\rangle$ of a prepared state $\\rho$ is therefore the average of $\\langle G\\rangle_\\rho$ over a uniformly random stabilizer $G$, and every $G$ has ideal value $+1$. Measuring one $G$ needs only single-qubit rotations before readout, and its value in each shot is a sign times the parity of the measured bits on its support. A few sampled stabilizers give an estimate of the fidelity whose uncertainty shrinks with the number of samples, so the benchmark stays verifiable at any qubit count. Because the sampled stabilizers carry $X$ and $Y$ factors as well as $Z$, the estimate responds to phase errors as well as bit flips.\n"
msgstr "Muatan menyediakan keadaan penstabil $|\\psi\\rangle = U|0\\rangle^{\\otimes n}$, dan unjurannya ialah purata $2^n$ unsur bertanda kumpulan penstabilnya, $|\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi| = 2^{-n} \\sum_G G$. Oleh itu fideliti $\\langle\\psi|\\rho|\\psi\\rangle$ bagi keadaan $\\rho$ yang disediakan ialah purata $\\langle G\\rangle_\\rho$ ke atas penstabil $G$ rawak seragam, dan setiap $G$ mempunyai nilai ideal $+1$. Mengukur satu $G$ hanya memerlukan putaran satu-qubit sebelum bacaan, dan nilainya dalam setiap shot ialah tanda didarab pariti bit terukur pada sokongannya. Beberapa penstabil yang disampel memberikan anggaran fideliti yang ketidakpastiannya mengecil dengan bilangan sampel, jadi penanda aras kekal boleh disahkan pada sebarang bilangan qubit. Oleh sebab penstabil yang disampel membawa faktor $X$ dan $Y$ serta $Z$, anggaran itu bertindak balas terhadap ralat fasa dan juga pembalikan bit.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<Admonition type=\"note\" title=\"A note on the word &quot;fidelity&quot; in this section\">\n"
msgstr "<Admonition type=\"note\" title=\"Catatan tentang perkataan &quot;fideliti&quot; dalam bahagian ini\">\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For the bare circuits (B0), the average of $\\langle G\\rangle$ over the sampled stabilizers estimates the fidelity of the prepared state. Ten samples give a rough estimate, whose uncertainty depends on both shot noise and variation between the sampled stabilizers. For the checked layouts it does not, even before post-selection. Their checks are chosen separately for every stabilizer, so the data need not be in the same state across the measurement settings. A check can preserve the ideal measurement statistics without preserving the full data state, as noted for the one-sided example. We therefore read both the raw and the post-selected averages of the checked layouts as benchmarks of expectation values, observable by observable, and not as the fidelity of one state.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"Bagi litar kosong (B0), purata $\\langle G\\rangle$ ke atas penstabil yang disampel menganggarkan fideliti keadaan yang disediakan. Sepuluh sampel memberikan anggaran kasar, yang ketidakpastiannya bergantung pada hingar shot dan juga variasi antara penstabil yang disampel. Bagi susun atur dengan semakan, ini tidak berlaku, walaupun sebelum pasca-pemilihan. Semakannya dipilih secara berasingan untuk setiap penstabil, jadi data tidak semestinya berada dalam keadaan yang sama merentas tetapan pengukuran. Sesuatu semakan boleh mengekalkan statistik pengukuran ideal tanpa mengekalkan keadaan data penuh, seperti yang dinyatakan untuk contoh satu-sisi. Oleh itu kami membaca purata mentah dan pasca-pilih bagi susun atur dengan semakan sebagai penanda aras nilai jangkaan, observabel demi observabel, dan bukan sebagai fideliti satu keadaan.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To test how the number of checks affects detection performance, we compare a ladder of check counts on every sampled stabilizer. All layouts share the payload, the data line, and the measurement, and they differ only in how many checks they add.\n"
msgstr "Untuk menguji bagaimana bilangan semakan mempengaruhi prestasi pengesanan, kami membandingkan tangga bilangan semakan pada setiap penstabil yang disampel. Semua susun atur berkongsi muatan, talian data, dan pengukuran, dan hanya berbeza dalam bilangan semakan yang ditambah.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "2.5.1 The layouts {#251-the-layouts}"
msgstr "2.5.1 Susun atur {#251-the-layouts}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For every sampled stabilizer $G$, `add_pauli_checks` runs the search of [Section 2.4](#paulice) on the circuit that measures $G$, with the targets in the order found there for $G_0$, from the best single check down. It commits one check per target and returns the circuit after each commitment, so one call per stabilizer gives the whole ladder. The important question is how many committed checks to keep.\n"
msgstr "Bagi setiap penstabil $G$ yang disampel, `add_pauli_checks` menjalankan carian [Bahagian 2.4](#paulice) pada litar yang mengukur $G$, dengan sasaran dalam susunan yang ditemui di sana untuk $G_0$, daripada semakan tunggal terbaik ke bawah. Ia mengomit satu semakan bagi setiap sasaran dan mengembalikan litar selepas setiap komit, jadi satu panggilan bagi setiap penstabil memberikan keseluruhan tangga. Soalan pentingnya ialah berapa banyak semakan yang dikomit untuk disimpan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The layouts are B0, P1, P2, P4, and the last P layout: zero, one, two, and four committed checks, and all of them. The name gives the check count. The last layout keeps every check the search commits, as the tutorial does, and its count depends on how many data qubits have a usable free neighbor. Reading the ladder in order compares successive check-augmented implementations, with B0, the unchecked circuit returned by the search, as the control.\n"
msgstr "Susun atur ialah B0, P1, P2, P4, dan susun atur P terakhir: sifar, satu, dua, dan empat semakan yang dikomit, dan semuanya. Nama itu menunjukkan bilangan semakan. Susun atur terakhir menyimpan setiap semakan yang dikomit oleh carian, seperti dalam tutorial, dan bilangannya bergantung pada berapa banyak qubit data mempunyai jiran bebas yang boleh digunakan. Membaca tangga mengikut urutan membandingkan pelaksanaan beraugmen semakan yang berturutan, dengan B0, litar tanpa semakan yang dikembalikan oleh carian, sebagai kawalan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Each $G$ gets its own checks, because the search depends on the measured observable. The selected data line, committed checks, gate counts, and model scores depend on the backend and its calibration. Use the tables generated by the current run as the reference, and compare the hardware results within that run.\n"
msgstr "Setiap $G$ mendapat semakannya sendiri, kerana carian bergantung pada observabel yang diukur. Talian data yang dipilih, semakan yang dikomit, bilangan gate, dan skor model bergantung pada backend dan penentukurannya. Gunakan jadual yang dijana oleh larian semasa sebagai rujukan, dan bandingkan keputusan perkakasan dalam larian tersebut.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<Admonition type=\"note\" title=\"Availability note\">\n"
msgstr "<Admonition type=\"note\" title=\"Catatan ketersediaan\">\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"On a data line with few usable free neighbors, the search commits fewer than four checks. P4 is then dropped and the last P layout keeps the checks as they are. If one stabilizer commits fewer checks than the others, the ladder stops at that smaller count for all of them.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"Pada talian data dengan sedikit jiran bebas yang boleh digunakan, carian mengomit kurang daripada empat semakan. P4 kemudian digugurkan dan susun atur P terakhir menyimpan semakan seperti sedia ada. Jika satu penstabil mengomit semakan yang lebih sedikit daripada yang lain, tangga berhenti pada bilangan yang lebih kecil itu untuk kesemuanya.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "2.5.2 Comparing layouts without running {#252-comparing-layouts-without-running}"
msgstr "2.5.2 Membandingkan susun atur tanpa menjalankan {#252-comparing-layouts-without-running}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The table compares the layouts on two quantities available before any shot is taken, both averaged over the stabilizers. Compare gamma at each step with B0 and the preceding layout. A lower value indicates less uncovered noise under the model, and neither a monotonic decrease nor the highest value at B0 is guaranteed. The added two-qubit gates show the price. Each check couples its ancilla to its target at a few points, and because the ancilla is a neighbor of the target, no routing is needed.\n"
msgstr "Jadual membandingkan susun atur berdasarkan dua kuantiti yang tersedia sebelum sebarang shot diambil, kedua-duanya dipuratakan ke atas penstabil. Bandingkan gamma pada setiap langkah dengan B0 dan susun atur sebelumnya. Nilai yang lebih rendah menunjukkan kurang hingar yang tidak dilindungi di bawah model, dan tiada jaminan sama ada penurunan monotonik atau nilai tertinggi pada B0. Gate dua-qubit tambahan menunjukkan harganya. Setiap semakan menggandingkan ancilla-nya kepada sasarannya pada beberapa titik, dan oleh sebab ancilla ialah jiran sasaran, tiada penghalaan diperlukan.\n"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The addon models device noise as a sparse Pauli-Lindblad channel: a set of Pauli fault generators $P_k$, one per gate location and Pauli type, each with a rate $\\lambda_k$. For a two-qubit gate with calibrated error probability $p$, the error is split evenly over the 15 non-identity two-qubit Paulis, and each generator gets $\\lambda = -\\tfrac{1}{2}\\ln(1 - 2p/15)$. Propagating operators through the circuit sorts the generators into three groups: those that commute with every measured operator (harmless, since they cannot change the output), those that anti-commute with some check's propagated support (detected, since they flip a syndrome bit), and the remainder, the uncovered faults within the measurement lightcone. Gamma is:\n"
msgstr "Addon memodelkan hingar peranti sebagai saluran Pauli-Lindblad jarang: satu set penjana kesalahan Pauli $P_k$, satu bagi setiap lokasi gate dan jenis Pauli, masing-masing dengan kadar $\\lambda_k$. Bagi gate dua-qubit dengan kebarangkalian ralat tertentukur $p$, ralat dibahagikan sama rata ke atas 15 Pauli dua-qubit bukan identiti, dan setiap penjana mendapat $\\lambda = -\\tfrac{1}{2}\\ln(1 - 2p/15)$. Merambatkan operator melalui litar mengasingkan penjana kepada tiga kumpulan: yang kalis tukar tertib dengan setiap operator terukur (tidak berbahaya, kerana ia tidak boleh mengubah output), yang antikalis tukar tertib dengan sokongan terrambat sesetengah semakan (dikesan, kerana ia membalikkan bit sindrom), dan bakinya, kesalahan yang tidak dilindungi dalam kon cahaya pengukuran. Gamma ialah:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "$$\\gamma = \\exp\\Big(2 \\sum_{k\\,\\in\\,\\text{uncovered}} \\lambda_k\\Big),$$\n"
msgstr "$$\\gamma = \\exp\\Big(2 \\sum_{k\\,\\in\\,\\text{uncovered}} \\lambda_k\\Big),$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "the quasi-probability cost of the channel that would invert exactly that residual noise ([van den Berg, Minev, Kandala, and Temme, Nat. Phys. 2023](https://arxiv.org/abs/2201.09866)). For this convention, the usual PEC sampling cost scales as $\\gamma^2$, while post-selection has a separate acceptance cost $1/A$. $\\gamma = 1$ means no positive-rate generator remains uncovered within the measurement lightcone. Committing a check that covers generators of total rate $\\Lambda$ divides gamma by $e^{2\\Lambda}$, while the generators of the check's own gates that it leaves undetected multiply gamma back up. This multiplicative structure is why each well-placed check lowers gamma by its own factor, and why a check that adds more noise than it covers can raise it.\n"
msgstr "kos kuasi-kebarangkalian bagi saluran yang akan menyongsangkan dengan tepat hingar baki itu ([van den Berg, Minev, Kandala, dan Temme, Nat. Phys. 2023](https://arxiv.org/abs/2201.09866)). Bagi konvensyen ini, kos pensampelan PEC biasa berskala sebagai $\\gamma^2$, manakala pasca-pemilihan mempunyai kos penerimaan yang berasingan $1/A$. $\\gamma = 1$ bermakna tiada penjana berkadar positif yang kekal tidak dilindungi dalam kon cahaya pengukuran. Mengomit semakan yang meliputi penjana berkadar keseluruhan $\\Lambda$ membahagikan gamma dengan $e^{2\\Lambda}$, manakala penjana bagi gate milik semakan itu sendiri yang tidak dikesannya mendarabkan gamma kembali ke atas. Struktur pendaraban ini menjelaskan mengapa setiap semakan yang ditempatkan dengan baik menurunkan gamma dengan faktornya sendiri, dan mengapa semakan yang menambah lebih banyak hingar daripada yang dilindunginya boleh menaikkannya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Because the exponent accumulates hundreds of generator rates, absolute gamma is exponentially sensitive to the calibration scale. A modest change in the per-gate error rate raises gamma to a power, so values can differ substantially between backends and between calibration days. Compare gammas only within a single run on a single backend, where the ordering is what matters. When a linear, additive quantity is needed, use $\\ln\\gamma / 2 = \\sum_k \\lambda_k$, the uncovered rate budget; each check's contribution then reads off as a difference of $\\ln\\gamma$.\n"
msgstr "Oleh sebab eksponen mengumpulkan ratusan kadar penjana, gamma mutlak sangat peka secara eksponen terhadap skala penentukuran. Perubahan sederhana dalam kadar ralat setiap gate menaikkan gamma kepada suatu kuasa, jadi nilai boleh berbeza dengan ketara antara backend dan antara hari penentukuran. Bandingkan gamma hanya dalam satu larian pada satu backend, di mana susunan itulah yang penting. Apabila kuantiti linear dan tambahan diperlukan, gunakan $\\ln\\gamma / 2 = \\sum_k \\lambda_k$, bajet kadar yang tidak dilindungi; sumbangan setiap semakan kemudian dibaca sebagai perbezaan $\\ln\\gamma$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The noise model comes from `PauliceNoiseModel.from_backend(backend, data_line)`. Each data-line coupler keeps its own calibrated error, readout enters as the average over the data line, and the couplers a check adds get a typical rate, which is why [Section 2.4](#paulice) screens the actual ancilla couplers against the calibration.\n"
msgstr "Model hingar datang daripada `PauliceNoiseModel.from_backend(backend, data_line)`. Setiap penggandingan talian data mengekalkan ralat tertentukurnya sendiri, bacaan masuk sebagai purata ke atas talian data, dan penggandingan yang ditambah oleh semakan mendapat kadar tipikal, itulah sebabnya [Bahagian 2.4](#paulice) menyaring penggandingan ancilla sebenar berbanding penentukuran.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "2.5.3 Hardware results {#253-hardware-results}"
msgstr "2.5.3 Keputusan perkakasan {#253-hardware-results}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The addon inserts its checks on the transpiled circuit, so it returns each layout as a ready-to-run [ISA circuit](/guides/transpile#instruction-set-architecture): payload, check ancillas, and measurements, already placed on physical qubits. Every circuit therefore goes to hardware exactly as scored, with no further transpilation (because re-routing would move the checks off the qubits the search chose). Submit all circuits in one job and wait for completion before proceeding.\n"
msgstr "Addon memasukkan semakannya pada litar yang ditranspil, jadi ia mengembalikan setiap susun atur sebagai [litar ISA](/guides/transpile#instruction-set-architecture) sedia dijalankan: muatan, ancilla semakan, dan pengukuran, yang sudah ditempatkan pada qubit fizikal. Oleh itu setiap litar dihantar ke perkakasan tepat seperti yang diskor, tanpa transpilasi lanjut (kerana penghalaan semula akan mengalihkan semakan daripada qubit yang dipilih oleh carian). Hantar semua litar dalam satu job dan tunggu sehingga selesai sebelum meneruskan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The submitted circuits retain their check rules, sampled stabilizers, and model scores in metadata. When retrieving a job, use these saved definitions. Repeating the search can change the checks and must not change how an earlier job is analyzed.\n"
msgstr "Litar yang dihantar mengekalkan peraturan semakan, penstabil yang disampel, dan skor model dalam metadata. Apabila mendapatkan semula job, gunakan takrifan tersimpan ini. Mengulangi carian boleh mengubah semakan dan tidak boleh mengubah cara job terdahulu dianalisis.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The following explains how the post-selection works. Each circuit measures the data qubits into register `meas` and the check ancillas into register `checks_c`. Each check contributes one syndrome bit per shot, the XOR of the measured bits of the qubits in its `check_support`; `0` means the comparison came out clean and `1` means the check fired. `cc.get_postselection_method()` returns the rule that reads this record. We rebuild it from the check definitions and the register and measurement map saved with each circuit, then pass it the bitstring from `join_data()` in that circuit's register order, and a shot is kept only when no check fired. The value of $G$ in a shot is its sign times the parity of the data bits on its support, as described above.\n"
msgstr "Yang berikut menerangkan bagaimana pasca-pemilihan berfungsi. Setiap litar mengukur qubit data ke dalam daftar `meas` dan ancilla semakan ke dalam daftar `checks_c`. Setiap semakan menyumbang satu bit sindrom bagi setiap shot, iaitu XOR bit terukur bagi qubit dalam `check_support`-nya; `0` bermakna perbandingan menghasilkan keputusan bersih dan `1` bermakna semakan itu terpicu. `cc.get_postselection_method()` mengembalikan peraturan yang membaca rekod ini. Kami membinanya semula daripada takrifan semakan serta daftar dan peta pengukuran yang disimpan bersama setiap litar, kemudian memberikannya rentetan bit daripada `join_data()` mengikut susunan daftar litar itu, dan sesuatu shot hanya disimpan apabila tiada semakan yang terpicu. Nilai $G$ dalam sesuatu shot ialah tandanya didarab pariti bit data pada sokongannya, seperti yang diterangkan di atas.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The table reports the following metrics for each layout:\n"
msgstr "Jadual melaporkan metrik berikut bagi setiap susun atur:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Column | Meaning |\n"
"|:-------|:--------|\n"
"| `layout` | B0 has no checks; P1, P2, P4, and the last P layout hold that many committed checks |\n"
"| `checks` | Number of checks per circuit |\n"
"| `gamma` | The addon's residual-noise cancellation cost estimate from Section 2.5.2 |\n"
"| `added 2Q gates` | Two-qubit gates added to the unchecked circuit |\n"
"| `A` | *Post-selection rate*: fraction of shots passing all checks (1.0 = no checks) |\n"
"| `1/A` | *Sampling overhead*: how many raw shots are needed per accepted shot |\n"
"| `raw` | Mean signed $\\langle G\\rangle$ over all shots, before post-selection |\n"
"| `post` | Mean signed $\\langle G\\rangle$ over the accepted shots only |\n"
"| `raw_ci`, `post_ci` | 95% half-widths from shot noise, for this fixed set of stabilizers |\n"
"| `gain vs B0` | `post` minus the `raw` value of B0 for the same stabilizer |\n"
"| `gain_se` | Standard error of that gain across the sampled stabilizers |\n"
msgstr ""
"| Lajur | Maksud |\n"
"|:-------|:--------|\n"
"| `layout` | B0 tiada semakan; P1, P2, P4, dan susun atur P terakhir mempunyai bilangan semakan yang dikomit sebanyak itu |\n"
"| `checks` | Bilangan semakan bagi setiap litar |\n"
"| `gamma` | Anggaran kos pembatalan hingar baki addon daripada Bahagian 2.5.2 |\n"
"| `added 2Q gates` | Gate dua-qubit yang ditambah pada litar tanpa semakan |\n"
"| `A` | *Kadar pasca-pemilihan*: pecahan shot yang melepasi semua semakan (1.0 = tiada semakan) |\n"
"| `1/A` | *Overhed pensampelan*: berapa banyak shot mentah diperlukan bagi setiap shot yang diterima |\n"
"| `raw` | Min $\\langle G\\rangle$ bertanda ke atas semua shot, sebelum pasca-pemilihan |\n"
"| `post` | Min $\\langle G\\rangle$ bertanda ke atas shot yang diterima sahaja |\n"
"| `raw_ci`, `post_ci` | Separuh lebar 95% daripada hingar shot, untuk set penstabil tetap ini |\n"
"| `gain vs B0` | `post` tolak nilai `raw` B0 bagi penstabil yang sama |\n"
"| `gain_se` | Ralat piawai bagi perolehan itu merentas penstabil yang disampel |\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Rates and values are averaged over the ten sampled stabilizers; `1/A` uses the averaged `A`.\n"
msgstr "Kadar dan nilai dipuratakan ke atas sepuluh penstabil yang disampel; `1/A` menggunakan `A` yang telah dipuratakan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Read the table along the check count, and compare the following two things measured on hardware:\n"
msgstr "Baca jadual mengikut bilangan semakan, dan bandingkan dua perkara berikut yang diukur pada perkakasan:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "*1. Whether the post-selected value improves, and at what cost in post-selection rate.* Each added check can cover more faults, but it also adds gates, and the search commits the best check it finds for each target in turn, even when that check raises gamma. Neither `post` nor gamma is guaranteed to improve at every step, so compare each change in `post` with the measured `A` and the uncertainty of the gain.\n"
msgstr "*1. Sama ada nilai pasca-pilih bertambah baik, dan pada kos kadar pasca-pemilihan sebanyak mana.* Setiap semakan tambahan boleh melindungi lebih banyak kesalahan, tetapi ia juga menambah gate, dan carian mengomit semakan terbaik yang ditemuinya bagi setiap sasaran secara bergilir, walaupun semakan itu menaikkan gamma. Tiada jaminan `post` atau gamma bertambah baik pada setiap langkah, jadi bandingkan setiap perubahan dalam `post` dengan `A` yang diukur dan ketidakpastian perolehan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "*2. How the raw value changes as checks are added.* The added gates can introduce errors, so compare both `raw` and `post` with the raw value of B0. A gain over the checked layout's own raw value is not enough by itself to establish a benefit over running the bare circuit.\n"
msgstr "*2. Bagaimana nilai mentah berubah apabila semakan ditambah.* Gate tambahan boleh memperkenalkan ralat, jadi bandingkan kedua-dua `raw` dan `post` dengan nilai mentah B0. Perolehan berbanding nilai mentah susun atur bersemakan itu sendiri tidak mencukupi dengan sendirinya untuk membuktikan faedah berbanding menjalankan litar kosong.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In the saved run, raw means decrease along the check ladder, while all post-selected point estimates exceed B0. The checked circuits therefore start from lower raw values, and the improvement appears after filtering. Compare the paired gains and their uncertainty before judging the benefit of each layout.\n"
msgstr "Dalam larian yang disimpan, min mentah menurun di sepanjang tangga semakan, manakala semua anggaran titik pasca-pilih melebihi B0. Oleh itu litar bersemakan bermula daripada nilai mentah yang lebih rendah, dan peningkatan muncul selepas penapisan. Bandingkan perolehan berpasangan dan ketidakpastiannya sebelum menilai faedah setiap susun atur.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/tools-for-quantum-advantage/error-correction-i/extracted-outputs/31ee3295-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/tools-for-quantum-advantage/error-correction-i/extracted-outputs/31ee3295-0.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In the left panel, faded bars show the raw mean of $\\langle G\\rangle$, solid bars show the post-selected mean, and the dashed line marks the bare baseline. The right panel shows the trade-off between post-selected mean and acceptance.\n"
msgstr "Dalam panel kiri, bar pudar menunjukkan min mentah $\\langle G\\rangle$, bar pepejal menunjukkan min pasca-pilih, dan garis putus-putus menandakan garis dasar kosong. Panel kanan menunjukkan pertukar-ganti antara min pasca-pilih dan kadar penerimaan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In the saved run, the post-selected mean rises along the check ladder while acceptance falls. The layout with all committed checks gives the highest post-selected mean and the lowest accepted-shot yield. This ordering agrees with decreasing gamma in the model table, but it does not establish which layout is best for every application.\n"
msgstr "Dalam larian yang disimpan, min pasca-pilih meningkat di sepanjang tangga semakan manakala kadar penerimaan menurun. Susun atur dengan semua semakan yang dikomit memberikan min pasca-pilih tertinggi dan hasil shot diterima terendah. Susunan ini selaras dengan gamma yang menurun dalam jadual model, tetapi ia tidak menentukan susun atur mana yang terbaik untuk setiap aplikasi.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Gamma is a model score computed without experimental shots, not a guarantee of hardware performance. Agreement gives a rough check of its ranking for these sampled observables, and another backend or calibration can produce a different ordering. Compare the gain, its uncertainty, acceptance, and added circuit cost when choosing a layout.\n"
msgstr "Gamma ialah skor model yang dikira tanpa shot eksperimen, bukan jaminan prestasi perkakasan. Persetujuan memberikan semakan kasar bagi kedudukannya untuk observabel yang disampel ini, dan backend atau penentukuran lain boleh menghasilkan susunan yang berbeza. Bandingkan perolehan, ketidakpastiannya, kadar penerimaan, dan kos litar tambahan apabila memilih susun atur.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "2.5.4 Interpretation {#254-interpretation}"
msgstr "2.5.4 Tafsiran {#254-interpretation}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The saved run illustrates the central trade-off of post-selected QEC: accepting fewer shots can improve agreement with the ideal observable values. Every checked layout improves on its own raw mean, and the all-check layout gives the largest post-selected gain over B0. Every checked raw mean is below B0 in this run, so the improvement over bare appears only after filtering.\n"
msgstr "Larian yang disimpan menggambarkan pertukar-ganti utama QEC pasca-pilih: menerima lebih sedikit shot boleh memperbaiki persetujuan dengan nilai observabel yang ideal. Setiap susun atur bersemakan memperbaiki min mentahnya sendiri, dan susun atur semua-semakan memberikan perolehan pasca-pilih terbesar berbanding B0. Setiap min mentah bersemakan berada di bawah B0 dalam larian ini, jadi peningkatan berbanding kosong hanya muncul selepas penapisan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This is the same principle used in the spacetime-code demonstration cited in the introduction, but that demonstration's tenfold figure concerns effective gate error rates. Our observable-by-observable benchmark measures a different quantity and does not reproduce that numerical claim.\n"
msgstr "Ini ialah prinsip yang sama yang digunakan dalam demonstrasi kod ruang-masa yang dipetik dalam pengenalan, tetapi angka sepuluh kali ganda dalam demonstrasi itu berkaitan kadar ralat gate berkesan. Penanda aras observabel demi observabel kami mengukur kuantiti yang berbeza dan tidak menghasilkan semula tuntutan berangka itu.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Report acceptance $A$ alongside the post-selected mean and the uncertainty of the paired gain. The sampling overhead $1/A$ and added gates determine the cost of obtaining accepted shots; more checks need not improve that trade-off. Both the values and their ordering can change with backend calibration, and the model's gamma ranking need not match the hardware ranking.\n"
msgstr "Laporkan kadar penerimaan $A$ bersama min pasca-pilih dan ketidakpastian perolehan berpasangan. Overhed pensampelan $1/A$ dan gate tambahan menentukan kos mendapatkan shot yang diterima; lebih banyak semakan tidak semestinya memperbaiki pertukar-ganti itu. Kedua-dua nilai dan susunannya boleh berubah mengikut penentukuran backend, dan kedudukan gamma model tidak semestinya sepadan dengan kedudukan perkakasan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Check your understanding {#check-your-understanding-7}"
msgstr "Semak kefahaman anda {#check-your-understanding-7}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Two layouts use the same qubit layout. One has no checks (acceptance rate = 1.0); the other has multiple checks (lower acceptance rate). The checked layout shows a higher post-selected value of $\\langle G\\rangle$. Which layout is better?\n"
msgstr "Dua susun atur menggunakan susun atur qubit yang sama. Satu tidak mempunyai semakan (kadar penerimaan = 1.0); satu lagi mempunyai beberapa semakan (kadar penerimaan lebih rendah). Susun atur bersemakan menunjukkan nilai $\\langle G\\rangle$ pasca-pilih yang lebih tinggi. Susun atur manakah yang lebih baik?\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "*It depends on the application.*\n"
msgstr "*Ia bergantung pada aplikasi.*\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "If the goal is accurate individual samples, for example in sampling-based algorithms where each accepted shot is a single-shot output, the checked layout might be preferable. Its accepted shots agree more often with the ideal value of the measured observable, and each kept shot is a sample, not a statistical reconstruction. This single-shot property is what distinguishes error detection from error mitigation. A higher post-selected $\\langle G\\rangle$ alone does not show that each accepted shot comes from a higher-fidelity state, because a check can change the data state without changing the statistics of $G$.\n"
msgstr "Jika matlamatnya ialah sampel individu yang tepat, contohnya dalam algoritma berasaskan pensampelan di mana setiap shot yang diterima ialah output satu-shot, susun atur bersemakan mungkin lebih baik. Shot yang diterimanya lebih kerap bersetuju dengan nilai ideal observabel yang diukur, dan setiap shot yang disimpan ialah satu sampel, bukan pembinaan semula statistik. Sifat satu-shot ini membezakan pengesanan ralat daripada pengurangan ralat. $\\langle G\\rangle$ pasca-pilih yang lebih tinggi sahaja tidak menunjukkan bahawa setiap shot yang diterima datang daripada keadaan berfideliti lebih tinggi, kerana semakan boleh mengubah keadaan data tanpa mengubah statistik $G$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "If the goal is many samples quickly and lower per-shot accuracy is acceptable (for example, for estimating expectation values), the unchecked layout may be more practical, because it produces more usable shots from the same batch.\n"
msgstr "Jika matlamatnya ialah banyak sampel dengan cepat dan ketepatan setiap shot yang lebih rendah boleh diterima (contohnya, untuk menganggar nilai jangkaan), susun atur tanpa semakan mungkin lebih praktikal, kerana ia menghasilkan lebih banyak shot yang boleh digunakan daripada kumpulan yang sama.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "*A useful shorthand for comparing layouts.* A layout with post-selection rate $A$ keeps about $A N$ of $N$ raw shots, so it needs $1/A$ times as many raw shots for the same number of accepted shots. Equal accepted counts give equal precision only if the observable's variance among the accepted shots is also similar. Set that cost against the gap between the post-selected value and the raw value of the bare layout. Comparing layouts on both numbers illustrates that more checks do not always win.\n"
msgstr "*Ringkasan berguna untuk membandingkan susun atur.* Susun atur dengan kadar pasca-pemilihan $A$ menyimpan kira-kira $A N$ daripada $N$ shot mentah, jadi ia memerlukan $1/A$ kali ganda shot mentah untuk bilangan shot diterima yang sama. Bilangan diterima yang sama memberikan ketepatan yang sama hanya jika varians observabel dalam kalangan shot yang diterima juga serupa. Bandingkan kos itu dengan jurang antara nilai pasca-pilih dan nilai mentah susun atur kosong. Membandingkan susun atur pada kedua-dua nombor menggambarkan bahawa lebih banyak semakan tidak selalu menang.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "*Caveat: error detection is not unbiased.*\n"
msgstr "*Peringatan: pengesanan ralat tidak saksama.*\n"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Post-selection removes the errors the checks detect, but not all errors. Faults that commute with every check or that occur outside any check's detection region pass through undetected. The post-selected distribution therefore remains *biased*: post-selection can reduce the bias, but it guarantees neither an improvement nor its complete removal. For tasks that require unbiased estimates of observables, error detection has to be combined with other error mitigation techniques (for example, probabilistic error cancellation on the post-selected data). The three relevant axes are:\n"
msgstr "Pasca-pemilihan membuang ralat yang dikesan oleh semakan, tetapi bukan semua ralat. Kesalahan yang kalis tukar tertib dengan setiap semakan atau yang berlaku di luar kawasan pengesanan mana-mana semakan melepasi tanpa dikesan. Taburan pasca-pilih itu oleh itu kekal *berat sebelah*: pasca-pemilihan boleh mengurangkan kebiasan, tetapi ia tidak menjamin peningkatan mahupun penyingkirannya sepenuhnya. Bagi tugas yang memerlukan anggaran observabel yang tidak berat sebelah, pengesanan ralat perlu digabungkan dengan teknik pengurangan ralat yang lain (contohnya, pembatalan ralat kebarangkalian pada data pasca-pilih). Tiga paksi yang berkaitan ialah:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "*Bias*: detection can reduce it, with no guarantee of a reduction or of its complete removal;\n"
msgstr "*Kebiasan*: pengesanan boleh mengurangkannya, tanpa jaminan pengurangan atau penyingkirannya sepenuhnya;\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "*Variance*: at comparable per-shot variance, fewer accepted shots mean higher statistical noise per estimate;\n"
msgstr "*Varians*: pada varians setiap shot yang setanding, lebih sedikit shot yang diterima bermakna hingar statistik yang lebih tinggi bagi setiap anggaran;\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "*Cost*: checks add gates, and rejected shots reduce the usable yield.\n"
msgstr "*Kos*: semakan menambah gate, dan shot yang ditolak mengurangkan hasil yang boleh digunakan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Design must consider all three of these.\n"
msgstr "Reka bentuk mesti mempertimbangkan ketiga-tiga perkara ini.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Wrap-up {#wrap-up}"
msgstr "Rumusan {#wrap-up}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This lesson covered error detection in quantum circuits through two complementary approaches that differ in where and how checks are placed. Part 1 focused on end-of-circuit detection (checks applied after the circuit completes), while Part 2 developed mid-circuit detection (checks placed at interior points during circuit execution).\n"
msgstr "Pelajaran ini merangkumi pengesanan ralat dalam litar kuantum melalui dua pendekatan pelengkap yang berbeza dari segi tempat dan cara semakan diletakkan. Bahagian 1 menumpukan pada pengesanan di hujung litar (semakan dikenakan selepas litar selesai), manakala Bahagian 2 membangunkan pengesanan pertengahan litar (semakan diletakkan pada titik dalaman semasa pelaksanaan litar).\n"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "*Part 1: End-of-circuit detection* demonstrated two strategies. Symmetry post-selection ([Section 1.1](#symmetry-post-selection)) uses known output constraints, like GHZ's two-bitstring support, to filter corrupted shots in classical post-processing, requiring no extra qubits but only catching errors visible in the final measurement basis. Stabilizer-code post-selection ([Section 1.2](#stabilizer-code)) adds ancilla qubits and syndrome extraction at the circuit's end, detecting both bit-flip and phase-flip errors through the $[[4,2,2]]$ code. The key limitation: all check information is collected at the final boundary, so the syndrome cannot localize when or where faults occurred during execution.\n"
msgstr "*Bahagian 1: Pengesanan di hujung litar* menunjukkan dua strategi. Pasca-pemilihan simetri ([Seksyen 1.1](#symmetry-post-selection)) menggunakan kekangan output yang diketahui, seperti sokongan dua rentetan bit GHZ, untuk menapis shot yang rosak dalam pemprosesan pasca klasik, tanpa memerlukan qubit tambahan tetapi hanya menangkap ralat yang kelihatan dalam asas pengukuran akhir. Pasca-pemilihan kod penstabil ([Seksyen 1.2](#stabilizer-code)) menambah qubit ancilla dan pengekstrakan sindrom di hujung litar, mengesan kedua-dua ralat pembalikan bit dan pembalikan fasa melalui kod $[[4,2,2]]$. Had utamanya: semua maklumat semakan dikumpulkan pada sempadan akhir, jadi sindrom tidak dapat menetapkan bila atau di mana kesalahan berlaku semasa pelaksanaan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "*Part 2: Mid-circuit detection* moved checks inside the circuit to access errors as they happen. Throughout, mid-circuit refers to where a check's detection region reaches, the circuit interior; the ancillas themselves are read out at the end alongside the data, with no dynamic-circuit operations. Coherent Pauli checks (Sections [2.2](#coherent)-[2.3](#spacetime)) provided the algebraic foundation: for any Clifford circuit $U$, the relation $L = U^\\dagger R\\, U$ defines valid check pairs, with detection via anti-commutation. The 20-qubit random Clifford payload provides a benchmark for testing whether the detection benefit outweighs the noise from added gates and routing. Spacetime codes (Sections [2.4](#paulice)-[2.5](#hardware-experiment)) refined this by placing lightweight checks where the circuit structure naturally supports them, with no $L$ needed, and tracing each check's *detection region* backward through the circuit. The `qiskit-paulice` addon automates that search and ranks placements by their model cost for residual noise. Sections [2.4](#paulice)-[2.5](#hardware-experiment) use a deeper version of the same circuit construction and compare checks through sampled stabilizers, weighing the post-selected gain of each added check against the acceptance it costs.\n"
msgstr "*Bahagian 2: Pengesanan pertengahan litar* memindahkan semakan ke dalam litar untuk mengakses ralat semasa ia berlaku. Sepanjang bahagian ini, pertengahan litar merujuk kepada tempat kawasan pengesanan sesuatu semakan sampai, iaitu bahagian dalam litar; ancilla itu sendiri dibaca di hujung bersama-sama data, tanpa operasi litar dinamik. Semakan Pauli koheren (Bahagian [2.2](#coherent)-[2.3](#spacetime)) menyediakan asas algebra: bagi sebarang litar Clifford $U$, hubungan $L = U^\\dagger R\\, U$ mentakrifkan pasangan semakan yang sah, dengan pengesanan melalui anti-kekalisan. Muatan Clifford rawak 20-qubit menyediakan penanda aras untuk menguji sama ada faedah pengesanan melebihi hingar daripada gate dan penghalaan tambahan. Kod ruang-masa (Bahagian [2.4](#paulice)-[2.5](#hardware-experiment)) memperhalusi ini dengan meletakkan semakan ringan di tempat struktur litar menyokongnya secara semula jadi, tanpa memerlukan $L$, dan menjejaki *kawasan pengesanan* setiap semakan ke belakang melalui litar. Addon `qiskit-paulice` mengautomasikan carian itu dan menyusun kedudukan penempatan mengikut kos model bagi hingar baki. Bahagian [2.4](#paulice)-[2.5](#hardware-experiment) menggunakan versi yang lebih dalam bagi pembinaan litar yang sama dan membandingkan semakan melalui penstabil yang disampel, menimbang perolehan pasca-pilih setiap semakan tambahan berbanding kadar penerimaan yang dikorbankannya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This lesson intentionally does not apply error mitigation or suppression techniques (for example, dynamical decoupling, readout error mitigation, or ZNE) that could further improve the results. The goal is to isolate the effect of error *detection* alone. Martiel & Javadi-Abhari report fidelity gains up to 236$\\times$ in their spacetime-check experiments, which also use dynamical decoupling and readout folding.\n"
msgstr "Pelajaran ini sengaja tidak menggunakan teknik pengurangan atau penindasan ralat (contohnya, dynamical decoupling, pengurangan ralat bacaan, atau ZNE) yang boleh memperbaiki lagi keputusan. Matlamatnya ialah mengasingkan kesan pengesanan ralat *semata-mata*. Martiel & Javadi-Abhari melaporkan perolehan fideliti sehingga 236$\\times$ dalam eksperimen semakan ruang-masa mereka, yang turut menggunakan dynamical decoupling dan readout folding.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "*Limitations to consider.*\n"
msgstr "*Batasan yang perlu dipertimbangkan.*\n"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Spacetime checks are a *heuristic*. They do not catch all errors. Faults that commute with every check, or that occur outside any detection region, pass undetected. Post-selection can therefore reduce the bias of the results, but it guarantees neither an improvement nor the removal of every error. For unbiased estimation of observables, error detection should be combined with other quantum error mitigation techniques ([Martiel & Javadi-Abhari, Supp. I](https://arxiv.org/abs/2504.15725)).\n"
msgstr "Semakan ruang-masa ialah *heuristik*. Ia tidak menangkap semua ralat. Kesalahan yang kalis tukar tertib dengan setiap semakan, atau yang berlaku di luar mana-mana kawasan pengesanan, tidak dikesan. Oleh itu pasca-pemilihan boleh mengurangkan kebiasan keputusan, tetapi ia tidak menjamin peningkatan mahupun penyingkiran setiap ralat. Untuk anggaran observabel yang tidak berat sebelah, pengesanan ralat perlu digabungkan dengan teknik pengurangan ralat kuantum yang lain ([Martiel & Javadi-Abhari, Supp. I](https://arxiv.org/abs/2504.15725)).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The checks are most effective for *Clifford-dominated circuits*; the space of valid checks shrinks exponentially with non-Clifford content ([Martiel & Javadi-Abhari, Supp. V](https://arxiv.org/abs/2504.15725)).\n"
msgstr "Semakan paling berkesan untuk *litar yang didominasi Clifford*; ruang semakan yang sah mengecil secara eksponen dengan kandungan bukan Clifford ([Martiel & Javadi-Abhari, Supp. V](https://arxiv.org/abs/2504.15725)).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "A Pauli operator's overall phase becomes a *relative phase between the ancilla branches* when the operator is controlled, and may need compensation by a single-qubit gate on the ancilla wire. The one-sided example of Section 2.3.2 corrects a minus sign on $L$ this way, and general implementations must account for it.\n"
msgstr "Fasa keseluruhan operator Pauli menjadi *fasa relatif antara cabang ancilla* apabila operator itu dikawal, dan mungkin memerlukan pampasan oleh gate satu-qubit pada wayar ancilla. Contoh satu-sisi dalam Bahagian 2.3.2 membetulkan tanda tolak pada $L$ dengan cara ini, dan pelaksanaan umum mesti mengambil kira perkara ini.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Three concrete open directions follow from this lesson. First, Sections [2.4](#paulice) and [2.5](#hardware-experiment) apply the placement search to a ten-layer 20-qubit payload; how its runtime scales to deeper circuits on hundreds of qubits determines whether the approach is practical for larger utility-scale circuits. Second, Part 2 used a random Clifford circuit construction at two depths. A natural next step is to check how the detection benefit holds up on deeper circuits and on circuits with some non-Clifford content, such as QAOA or VQE ansatze. Third, spacetime codes here use syndrome information for post-selection rather than active correction, and their heuristic construction has no particular distance guarantee. Moving to fault-tolerant correction requires checks with suitable distance, fault-tolerant syndrome extraction, and a decoder.\n"
msgstr "Tiga hala tuju terbuka yang konkrit timbul daripada pelajaran ini. Pertama, Bahagian [2.4](#paulice) dan [2.5](#hardware-experiment) menggunakan carian penempatan pada muatan 20-qubit sepuluh lapisan; cara masa jalannya berskala kepada litar yang lebih dalam pada ratusan qubit menentukan sama ada pendekatan ini praktikal untuk litar berskala utiliti yang lebih besar. Kedua, Bahagian 2 menggunakan pembinaan litar Clifford rawak pada dua kedalaman. Langkah seterusnya yang wajar ialah menyemak sama ada manfaat pengesanan kekal pada litar yang lebih dalam dan pada litar yang mengandungi sedikit kandungan bukan Clifford, seperti ansatz QAOA atau VQE. Ketiga, kod ruang-masa di sini menggunakan maklumat sindrom untuk pasca-pemilihan dan bukannya pembetulan aktif, dan pembinaan heuristiknya tidak mempunyai jaminan jarak tertentu. Peralihan kepada pembetulan toleran-kesalahan memerlukan semakan dengan jarak yang sesuai, pengekstrakan sindrom toleran-kesalahan, dan sebuah penyahkod.\n"

